#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""Run coding agents in srt with persistent, per-project, per-agent homes.

Configuration (JSON with // and /* */ comments and trailing commas):
    ~/.config/srt-agent/config.jsonc   Global (or SRT_AGENT_SETTINGS / --settings)
    <project>/.srt-agent.jsonc         Per project; agents cannot change it
Every file is flat: srt's two lists, "network" and "filesystem", sit next
to the launcher's own keys. Only these srt lists are forwarded, and only
the listed names inside them (network: allowedDomains, deniedDomains,
allowUnixSockets, allowMachLookup; filesystem: allowRead, denyRead,
allowWrite, denyWrite). Any other key, at any level, is refused.
    global:  network, filesystem, crossSessionMessaging, passEnv, agents,
             autoVenv, toolsVenv, path, setEnv, groups, agentHome, baseSettings
    group:   network, filesystem, remove, path, setEnv
    agent:   network, filesystem, passEnv, setEnv, binary, homeEnv
    project: network, filesystem, remove, extends, path, setEnv, agentHome
srt-agent does not read ~/.srt-settings.json unless you import it
explicitly: "baseSettings": "~/.srt-settings.json" in the global config. Imported network/filesystem lists become inherited defaults
for every agent (merged first; a project's approved "remove" can drop them);
the file must be strict JSON with srt's list settings and switches only.
Its switches (allowAppleEvents, enableWeakerNestedSandbox,
enableWeakerNetworkIsolation, network.allowLocalBinding,
network.allowAllUnixSockets) are the first layer: the global config,
groups and the project may change them, and turning one on is asked
about. allowPty may appear only as true. Any other key is refused, never
ignored. Approval binds its parsed content; it is shown in
the approval diff and write-protected. Off by default. These are inherited
DEFAULTS, not a floor: an approved project "remove" can drop any imported
entry, deny rules included. Each launch passes
srt one complete generated policy with --settings. --check verifies
this: if ~/.srt-settings.json allows a domain the generated policy does
not, the sandbox proxy must refuse it (the file is read only for that test).
A denyRead that a read grant already covers (same path or inside it) is
refused: in srt allowRead wins, so such a block would do nothing. Literal
paths and glob blocks against literal grants are checked fully (as written
and with symlinks resolved); a glob grant is checked against each block's
literal part. Two globs that overlap only partly are not decided, so a block
that passes is not proven effective. The glob model mirrors srt's syntax
(* and ? within a folder name, ** across folders, [...] classes) but is the
launcher's own reading of it, not srt's matcher.
Parsing is strict after comments and trailing commas are removed:
duplicate keys, NaN/Infinity and stray commas are errors. Approvals bind
the parsed settings, so editing a comment does not ask again.

Usage after installation:
    srt-agent project init
    srt-agent project init -e lang/rust,restricted   (-e = --extends)
    srt-agent project approve
    srt-agent project revoke
    srt-agent run claude
    srt-agent run codex
    srt-agent run pi
    srt-agent run dsh                      (alias: deepseek)
    srt-agent run dsh -- --profile headless "run the tests"
    srt-agent run -l dsh -- web            (-l = --allow-local-binding)
    claude [Launcher options...] -- [Claude arguments...]
    codex [Launcher options...] -- [Codex arguments...]
    claude --resume [SESSION_ID]
    codex -- resume --last
    claude --allow-local-binding -- auth login
    claude --allow-cross-session-messaging
    claude --cross-session-messaging project
    claude --cross-session-messaging global
    claude --no-cross-session-messaging
    codex --allow-local-binding -- login
    claude --allow-home
    claude --no-pty-isolation
    srt-agent project init --allow-home
    srt-agent run --show claude
    srt-agent run --check claude
    srt-agent run --project /path/to/project codex
    srt-agent run --auto-venv claude
    srt-agent exec claude -- toolpy -c "import openpyxl"
    srt-agent exec claude                  (a shell with Claude's sandbox and env)
    srt-agent exec claude -- pytest -q
    srt-agent exec --allow-local-binding codex -- npm run dev

Aliases (use the literal installed path, not $HOME):
    alias claude='/Users/joyce/.local/bin/srt-agent run claude'
    alias codex='/Users/joyce/.local/bin/srt-agent run codex'
    alias pi='/Users/joyce/.local/bin/srt-agent run pi'
    alias dsh='/Users/joyce/.local/bin/srt-agent run dsh'

Built-in agents (binary, private config location, extra network domains):
    claude  claude  CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=<agent home>/.claude       (none)
    codex   codex   CODEX_HOME=<agent home>/.codex               OpenAI domains
    pi      pi      PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR=<agent home>/.pi/agent   (none: provider-specific)
    dsh     dsh     DSH_HOME=<agent home>/.dsh                   api.deepseek.com
Every agent's config variables are set for every launch, all inside the
running agent's own home. Other agents can be defined, or the built-ins
extended, in the global config (covered by approval):
    "passEnv": ["MY_SETTING"],
    "agents": {
      "pi":    {"network": {"allowedDomains": ["api.anthropic.com"]}, "passEnv": ["ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"]},
      "codex": {"filesystem": {"allowRead": ["/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/codex"]}},
      "my-agent": {"binary": "my-agent", "homeEnv": {"MY_AGENT_HOME": ".my-agent"},
                   "network": {"allowedDomains": ["api.example.com"]}, "passEnv": ["EXAMPLE_API_KEY"],
                   "setEnv": {"MY_AGENT_TELEMETRY": "0"}}
    }
"path" appends host tool folders to the agent PATH (readable, write-denied)
and "setEnv" sets variables (a leading ~/ means your account home). Both go
in the global config for every project, or in a project file for that
project alone; setEnv
precedence is global, then project, then the agent's. Rust via rustup, per
project (.srt-agent.jsonc in the project):
    "filesystem": {"allowRead": [".", "~/.rustup"], "allowWrite": ["."]},
    "path": ["~/.cargo/bin"], "setEnv": {"RUSTUP_HOME": "~/.rustup"}
Groups. Reusable sets defined once in the global settings and pulled into
a project with "extends"; groups merge in the order listed and the
project's own entries come last (lists add up, setEnv: later wins).
Groups take the project-override keys plus network.allowedDomains, and
"remove" revokes exact global entries (domains included):
    global:  "groups": {
               "rust": {"filesystem": {"allowRead": ["~/.rustup"]},
                        "network": {"allowedDomains": ["crates.io", "index.crates.io", "static.crates.io"]},
                        "path": ["~/.cargo/bin"], "setEnv": {"RUSTUP_HOME": "~/.rustup"}},
               "restricted": {"remove": {"network": {"allowedDomains": ["github.com"]}}}}
    project: {"extends": ["rust", "restricted"],
              "filesystem": {"allowRead": ["."], "allowWrite": ["."]}}
Groups can also live in their own files, one per group, next to the
global config: ~/.config/srt-agent/groups/<name>.jsonc holds exactly what
a group holds (network, filesystem, remove, path, setEnv); the file name
is the group name. Hidden files and names not ending in .jsonc are
skipped; an invalid name is refused, as is a group defined both inline
and as a file. Symlinked files (stow) are followed. The folder and every
group file's target are write-denied to agents.
Group names may carry one namespace folder: groups/lang/php.jsonc is
"lang/php", groups/tool/rg.jsonc is "tool/rg".
Generating a group for programs:
    srt-agent group create --tool rg              -> groups/tool/rg.jsonc
    srt-agent group create dev --tool rg --tool fd
    srt-agent group update tool/rg                (after brew install/upgrade)
It grants the program's own files, its Homebrew formula and that formula's
runtime dependencies (from Homebrew's INSTALL_RECEIPT.json records), the
libraries it links (otool -L, following @rpath), and for scripts the
interpreter in the shebang, recursively. Nothing is executed. Whole
formula folders are granted, so upgrades keep working. Files a tool opens
only while running (config, plugins) cannot be seen; the sandbox log names
them on first use. An existing file is never replaced unless --force or
update is used; macOS's own programs need no group.
Template home: ~/.config/srt-agent/home/ mirrors an agent home and is
applied at every launch: common/ for every agent, then <agent>/ (which
wins), e.g. home/claude/.claude/CLAUDE.md, home/codex/.codex/AGENTS.md,
home/pi/.pi/agent/AGENTS.md.
    regular file        copied and write-protected ("managed"); rewritten
                        every launch, so agents cannot change their own
                        global instructions
    <agent>/.seed/...   copied only if missing, then the agent's to change
                        (e.g. .seed/.codex/config.toml)
    link to a file      recreated as a link, its target readable (not
                        writable): edits to the real file are live
A file the launcher did not write is kept as <name>.srt-agent-backup-<time>
before being replaced; files dropped from the template are removed if
unchanged. .local/bin and .claude/sessions are the launcher's own. The
template is part of the global settings: changing it asks every project
again (linked files are live, so only the link is approved). With
agentHome shared, two agents' templates may not both write a path.
Agent groups: groups/agent/<agent>.jsonc (e.g. agent/pi) is applied
automatically whenever that agent runs, in every project. It may hold
network.allowedDomains, filesystem.allowRead, path, setEnv and extends
(the groups it reaches are held to the same keys); the agent's entry in
config.jsonc wins on setEnv. Like that entry, it is part of the global
settings: changing an agent group, or a group it extends, asks every
project again. srt-agent group create agent/pi --tool pi generates one.
A group may itself "extends": ["other", ...]: those come first, in order,
then the group's own entries; a group reached through several paths is
applied once, where it first appears; cycles and unknown names are
refused for every launch, with the chain shown.
Switches: allowLocalBinding and allowAllUnixSockets (in network),
allowAppleEvents, enableWeakerNestedSandbox and enableWeakerNetworkIsolation
may be set in the imported srt file, the global config, groups and project
files; later layers win (project last), and --allow-local-binding turns
local binding on for one launch. allowPty may appear only as true; proxy
ports are never accepted. Project files may also list allowedDomains and
deniedDomains.
Loosening prompts: before the final approval, each kind of loosening since
the last approval gets its own question with the items listed: new
domains, removed domain blocks, new Unix sockets, new Mach services, new
read or write access (outside the project), removed read or write blocks,
and switches turned on. Answering no to any of them launches nothing.
Approval: an inline group is part of config.jsonc, so changing it asks
every project again. A group file is bound only to the projects that
extend it, directly or through another group: editing
groups/php-common.jsonc re-asks only projects that reach it, and the
approval prompt shows that file.
A setEnv value starting with {cache} names this project's own cache folder,
~/Library/Caches/srt-agent/<project>-<id>, created 0700 and writable only for
this project. It lies outside the project, where srt's built-in blocks on
.vscode/.idea/.git hooks do not apply, so crates that ship them unpack:
    "setEnv": {"RUSTUP_HOME": "~/.rustup", "CARGO_HOME": "{cache}/cargo", "TMPDIR": "{cache}/tmp"}
TMPDIR may be redirected, but only into {cache}: tests that create Git
repositories or rc files in temp folders need it. Delete that folder
yourself when you retire a project.
Without it, CARGO_HOME stays in the private HOME, so each project has its own crate
cache, and ~/.cargo (with credentials.toml) stays hidden.
network.allowedDomains and filesystem.allowRead (absolute or ~/ paths)
add to the sandbox only while that agent runs (srt settings layout).
A custom agent requires binary; homeEnv paths are relative to the private
HOME. For a built-in, the listed lists are appended and binary may be
replaced. SRT_AGENT_<AGENT> (upper-case, - as _) overrides the executable.

Environment is deny-by-default. Only terminal/locale variables, each
agent's documented settings (Claude: ANTHROPIC_*, CLAUDE_CODE_*; Codex:
OPENAI_*; dsh: DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, DSH_*; pi: PI_*) and names listed in
passEnv reach the sandbox. A trailing * matches a prefix. Cloud, GitHub,
SSH-agent and other host credentials are NOT inherited unless listed.
Launcher-managed names (PATH, HOME, TMPDIR, XDG_*, proxies, DYLD_*, LD_*,
...) cannot be passed or set.

Access to a project requires an explicit .srt-agent.jsonc in its root.
There is NO automatic current-directory allowance. project init explicitly creates:
    {"filesystem": {"allowRead": ["."], "allowWrite": ["."]}}
Relative override paths anchor at that project root, even from a subdirectory.
The project root is the nearest ancestor containing .git (found without
running git), otherwise the current directory.
Without an override the launcher refuses to start and creates no storage.
The override accepts filesystem.allowRead, allowWrite, denyRead and denyWrite,
network.allowedDomains, deniedDomains, allowUnixSockets and allowMachLookup,
and the switches listed above. Read paths and socket
paths may be external. ~/ is expanded to the REAL account home before HOME
changes. Write grants stay confined to this project. Denials may be external.
Root reads and wildcard Mach
names are rejected. Whole-home reads and starting from home require the
per-launch --allow-home flag plus the ordinary project approval. A home
project also uses .srt-agent.jsonc; the global config lives elsewhere.
A non-Git folder can also opt in. /root and the launcher itself are always
read/write-denied, regardless of project grants or --allow-home.
The project's .git/config, .git/hooks, a .git gitlink file, .envrc, .env
and .vscode are always write-denied: host-side Git, direnv, dotenv loaders
and VS Code (tasks, launch configs, settings that name executables) would
otherwise run commands planted there. Edit those files on the host.
Every directory on PATH, both your host PATH and the agent's own PATH
(including <agent home>/.local/bin), is write-denied too, so the agent can
never plant a command that a later lookup runs. Relative or empty host
PATH entries are resolved against the project; one that names the project
root or an ancestor is refused, because it would deny every project write.

Python virtualenvs. An activated venv (VIRTUAL_ENV from bin/activate, uv,
poetry shell, ...) is carried into the sandbox: VIRTUAL_ENV (and
VIRTUAL_ENV_PROMPT) are set, its bin comes first on the agent PATH, and
read access is granted to the venv and to the base interpreter named by
pyvenv.cfg and bin/python (never the home directory or an ancestor).
With --auto-venv, or global "autoVenv": true, a launch with
no VIRTUAL_ENV uses the project's own .venv (a real directory, not a
symlink). --no-auto-venv turns that off for one run; --no-venv ignores
every venv. Each venv's grants need interactive approval once; approved
venvs are remembered until the project settings change. A venv's bin and
pyvenv.cfg are write-denied (bin is on PATH), so install packages that add
commands on the host. A venv outside the project is read-only to the
agent. Conda (CONDA_PREFIX) is not detected.

Shared tools. Global "toolsVenv": "~/.local/share/srt-agent/tools"
names one host-maintained venv (e.g. openpyxl, pandas) for every project:
    /usr/bin/python3 -m venv ~/.local/share/srt-agent/tools
    ~/.local/share/srt-agent/tools/bin/pip install openpyxl pandas
It is read-only to every agent and must lie outside the project. Its bin
comes after the project venv but before system Pythons, so python3 has
its packages in projects without a venv. The launcher also writes a
toolpy wrapper into the private .local/bin that always runs it, even
where a project venv shadows python3. Its resolved read grants are part
of the global approval; an upgrade that moves its interpreter asks again.

exec AGENT [-- COMMAND...] runs COMMAND, or your $SHELL when omitted, under
exactly the sandbox, private HOME, PATH, venv and environment that
run AGENT would use, without the agent's own arguments or messaging.
New/modified global or project policies require interactive approval. Approval
binds both files' paths, exact bytes and resolved permissions. Records
live under the real ~/.local/state/srt-agent/approvals, write-denied to agents.
--show previews without approving; unattended launches fail if not approved.
Local listeners are disabled unless --allow-local-binding is supplied for
this invocation before the -- separator. It permits listeners and loopback,
which also reaches every host service listening on localhost; use it only
for logins or a web UI such as dsh web. It does not persist.
Global "crossSessionMessaging": "project" selects the default
communication scope: off (default), project, or global. true/false remain
aliases for project/off. --cross-session-messaging SCOPE overrides it for
one run. --allow-cross-session-messaging means project, and
--no-cross-session-messaging means off.
Project scope uses Claude's own <agent tmp>/run/cc-socks; global scope shares
only inboxes and discovery/auth records under the actual account's
~/.local/state/srt-agent-messaging. Global scope lets sessions in different
projects message each other, which weakens per-project isolation.
Credentials and other config stay in
Claude's own agent home. Messaging is Claude-only: other agents never get
a channel to Claude sessions. Each session gets its own socket in the selected directory.
An explicit --messaging-socket-path uses the short temp alias and a unique filename.
The launcher creates the real leaf directory before sandboxing, avoiding
Claude's default ancestor-walking setup through the temp symlink. It permits
only the selected socket directory's lexical and resolved paths, plus
the global registry in global mode. TCP listeners are unchanged. Sessions
must choose the same communication scope to reach one another.
The enable option cannot be combined with an agent --messaging-socket-path
override. The global default applies to Claude only; other agents are unaffected.
Claude's sessions directory switches between a preserved project registry
and the global registry. Switching registry scopes refuses live sessions
in the same project; exit them before switching. Host-side scope leases
are protected alongside approvals; stale leases are pruned on later runs.
Launcher keys never reach the generated srt policy. Approvals cover them
as part of the config file they are in.

Interactive launches run the agent on a fresh pseudo-terminal in a new
session (inside the sandbox). The agent cannot use TIOCSTI on your real
terminal to type commands into your shell after it exits. Job-control
suspend (Ctrl-Z) is resumed automatically. --no-pty-isolation disables it.

Agent storage lives outside the project, one folder per project:
    ~/.local/share/srt-agent/projects/<name>-<id>/
        project.json             Identity record (launcher-owned)
        agents/<agent>/home/     That agent's HOME: its credentials, config,
                                 CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/CODEX_HOME/XDG_* dirs
        agents/<agent>/tmp/      That agent's temporary files
        srt-tmp/<agent>/         srt's own host-side temp (agents: no access)
The identity record is a consistency check against reusing another
project's folder, not proof that the folder's contents are trustworthy.
<id> is 96 bits of SHA-256 of the resolved project path; renaming or moving
a project starts its agents fresh. Each agent may read and write only its
own home and tmp: not its agents/<agent> folder itself, not the identity
record, not other agents' folders, not other projects. Read grants cannot
be denied back once allowed, so any grant overlapping the storage or cache
roots is refused (except whole-home access with --allow-home, which
exposes every agent's storage and weakens cross-agent and cross-project
confidentiality). Delete a
retired project's folders yourself (storage and ~/Library/Caches/srt-agent).
"agentHome": "isolated" (default) or "shared", globally or in a project file
(approved like the rest), chooses whether this project's agents share one HOME
(<storage>/shared/home) or keep separate ones. Shared mode is mutual
trust: each agent can read the other's credentials AND change its
configuration (settings, hooks, instructions, Claude's sessions registry),
influencing the other's future sessions. Use it only for agents you trust
together. --show reports the effective mode. Temp folders, srt's temp and launcher-owned files stay separate;
other projects stay isolated. The two modes use different folders, so
switching never merges state: the other mode's homes are kept unchanged.
A nested agent (codex started inside a Claude session) uses config dirs
inside the CALLING agent's home, so it signs in separately from launching
that agent directly; this is deliberate.
Separate homes keep credentials apart, but agents of one project still
share its files and its {cache}: they are not isolated from each other's
work. The macOS Keychain is not isolated by HOME either.
Generated policies live in the protected
~/.local/state/srt-agent/policies/<project-hash>/<agent>-*.json.

Merges network and filesystem policy from the global config (SRT_AGENT_SETTINGS
or ~/.config/srt-agent/config.jsonc) with the explicit project override,
agent storage, agent executable and mandatory protections. System read
permissions come from the global config. Global ~/ paths refer to the REAL account home;
external global write exceptions are preserved. Global current-directory
grants are rejected; put them in the project override. Global allow globs
are expanded to concrete paths at launch and included in approval; deny
globs remain patterns. Does not modify the global config, install
itself, or edit shell profiles. Project overrides are created only when
project init is explicitly requested, and existing overrides are never replaced.
Generated policies are never reused as inputs. Their directory, the source
settings, and the launcher's lexical and resolved paths are write-denied.
Read denies include / and the absolute account home. Never put a literal ~
there: the agent runs with HOME changed to its private agent home.
The optional project remove object mirrors filesystem and network list names:
    {"filesystem": {"allowRead": ["."], "allowWrite": ["."]},
     "remove": {"filesystem": {"allowRead": ["~/.claude"]},
                "network": {"allowMachLookup": ["some.service"]}}}
Removals match original global entries exactly, before path expansion or
glob handling; unmatched entries are errors. All four filesystem lists and
the two IPC lists support removals. Removed global entries are followed by
project additions and mandatory protections; removals never suppress those.
An empty array adds/removes nothing. Approval includes removals. Removing
an allow is not a deny, and removing a deny is not an allow. Project paths
are literal; a glob-shaped removal names the exact global pattern to remove.
Does not copy host settings, credentials, hooks or plugins. macOS Keychain
is not isolated by HOME.

srt itself runs with your real HOME and a sanitized host PATH. The private
HOME, PATH and other agent variables are applied only inside the sandbox,
so nothing the agent writes into its storage is ever executed by srt.
Host-side steps inside agent-writable folders (wrapper install, Claude's
sessions link) use no-follow descriptor walks, so planted symlinks are refused.
Agent temp variables use the real agent tmp path, without a symlink.
A short, project-and-agent-specific /tmp symlink points INTO it for
XDG_RUNTIME_DIR; srt itself gets a separate alias to its own launcher-owned
temp folder, so the unsandboxed srt never uses a folder an agent could have
seeded. Both avoid macOS socket path limits; a stale alias of your own is
retargeted. No automatic cleanup.

Uses /usr/bin/python3 in isolated mode (3.9+) to avoid PATH or project Python
module shadowing. Requires macOS, srt, and installed agent binaries.
SRT_AGENT_SRT overrides the srt path. CLI options
for this launcher go before the first --; everything after that separator
is passed unchanged to the agent. Only Claude --resume [SESSION_ID] is also
accepted before -- as an explicit shorthand. No other agent flags are guessed.
Choose a project before starting; an agent --cd flag
does not expand the outer sandbox's permitted project.
"""

import argparse
import copy
import difflib
import errno
import fcntl
import glob
import hashlib
import json
import os
import pwd
from pathlib import Path
import re
import shlex
import shutil
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time


OPENAI_DOMAINS = [
    "chatgpt.com", "*.chatgpt.com", "openai.com", "*.openai.com",
    "*.oaistatic.com", "*.oaiusercontent.com",
]
# Built-in agent profiles. homeEnv paths are relative to the private HOME.
# passEnv names the host variables this agent documents for its own use.
AGENTS = {
    "claude": {
        "binary": "claude",
        "homeEnv": {"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR": ".claude"},
        "allowedDomains": [],
        "passEnv": ["ANTHROPIC_*", "CLAUDE_CODE_*", "DISABLE_*"],
        "setEnv": {},
        "messaging": True,
        "resumeShorthand": True,
        "prependArgs": [],
    },
    "codex": {
        "binary": "codex",
        "homeEnv": {"CODEX_HOME": ".codex"},
        "allowedDomains": OPENAI_DOMAINS,
        "passEnv": ["OPENAI_*"],
        "setEnv": {},
        # Current Codex can use a host-wide daemon. Keep this session's TUI and
        # model execution under srt instead of handing it to that host daemon.
        "prependArgs": ["--no-daemon"],
    },
    # pi (pi.dev) has no sandbox of its own. Its provider is user-selected,
    # so no API domain is assumed: add one under agents.pi.network.allowedDomains.
    "pi": {
        "binary": "pi",
        "homeEnv": {"PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR": ".pi/agent"},
        "allowedDomains": [],
        "passEnv": ["PI_*"],
        "setEnv": {},
        "prependArgs": [],
    },
    # DeepSeek Harness (@deepseek-ai/dsh). Telemetry goes to a separate
    # collector host that is deliberately not allowed; also switch it off.
    "dsh": {
        "binary": "dsh",
        "homeEnv": {"DSH_HOME": ".dsh"},
        "allowedDomains": ["api.deepseek.com"],
        "passEnv": ["DEEPSEEK_API_KEY", "DSH_*"],
        "setEnv": {"DSH_TELEMETRY_DISABLED": "1"},
        "prependArgs": [],
    },
}
AGENT_ALIASES = {"deepseek": "dsh"}
AGENT_NAME = re.compile(r"[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,23}\Z")
RESERVED_AGENT_NAMES = {"srt", "settings", "child-env", "pty"}
# Passed for every agent: terminal and locale presentation only.
BASE_PASS_ENV = [
    "TERM", "COLORTERM", "TERM_PROGRAM", "TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION", "TERMINFO",
    "LANG", "LANGUAGE", "LC_*", "TZ", "USER", "LOGNAME", "SHELL",
    "NO_COLOR", "FORCE_COLOR", "CLICOLOR", "CLICOLOR_FORCE", "COLUMNS", "LINES",
    "__CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING", "EDITOR", "VISUAL",
]
ENV_PATTERN = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\*?\Z")
ENV_NAME = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\Z")
FORBIDDEN_ENV = {
    "PATH", "HOME", "TMPDIR", "TMP", "TEMP", "ZDOTDIR", "BASH_ENV", "ENV",
    "SANDBOX_RUNTIME", "SRT_AGENT_CHILD_ENV", "SRT_AGENT_PTY", "SRT_DEBUG",
    "NODE_OPTIONS", "SSH_AUTH_SOCK", "PROMPT_COMMAND",
    "VIRTUAL_ENV", "VIRTUAL_ENV_PROMPT",
}
FORBIDDEN_ENV_PREFIXES = ("DYLD_", "LD_", "XDG_", "SRT_", "PYTHON")
PROXY_ENV = re.compile(r"(?i)(http|https|all|ftp|grpc|no|docker_http|docker_https)_proxy\Z")
# Unix sockets and services that act with your full host privileges.
RISKY_SOCKET_HINTS = ("docker", "podman", "colima", "orbstack", "lima", "ssh", "gpg",
                      "1password", "agent.sock", "launchd")
PROJECT_SETTINGS = ".srt-agent.jsonc"
# Older names: refused with rename instructions, never read.
GLOBAL_SETTINGS = Path(".config/srt-agent/config.jsonc")  # relative to the account home
TRUST_FORMAT = 5
REMOVABLE_LISTS = {
    "filesystem": ("allowRead", "allowWrite", "denyRead", "denyWrite"),
    "network": ("allowedDomains", "deniedDomains", "allowUnixSockets", "allowMachLookup"),
}
GROUP_SEGMENT = r"[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,63}"
# A group name may carry one namespace, e.g. "lang/php" or "tool/rg"; the
# file is then groups/lang/php.jsonc.
GROUP_NAME = re.compile(GROUP_SEGMENT + "(/" + GROUP_SEGMENT + ")?")
EXEC_CODE = r'''
import json, os, sys
from urllib.parse import urlsplit, urlunsplit
# The launcher hands agent variables through srt in one JSON value so that
# srt itself never runs with the agent-writable private HOME or PATH.
child = json.loads(os.environ.pop("SRT_AGENT_CHILD_ENV"))
isolate_pty = os.environ.pop("SRT_AGENT_PTY", "") == "1"
os.environ.update(child)
# srt sets these after the launcher starts. Use the numeric loopback address
# for its proxy so client token exchange does not depend on sandboxed DNS.
# Keep proxy authentication, port, scheme and upstream filtering unchanged.
for name in ("HTTP_PROXY", "HTTPS_PROXY", "ALL_PROXY", "FTP_PROXY", "GRPC_PROXY",
             "http_proxy", "https_proxy", "all_proxy", "ftp_proxy", "grpc_proxy",
             "DOCKER_HTTP_PROXY", "DOCKER_HTTPS_PROXY"):
    value = os.environ.get(name)
    if not value:
        continue
    try:
        parts = urlsplit(value)
        if parts.hostname != "localhost":
            continue
        credentials, separator, _ = parts.netloc.rpartition("@")
        address = (credentials + "@" if separator else "") + "127.0.0.1"
        if parts.port is not None:
            address += ":" + str(parts.port)
        os.environ[name] = urlunsplit((parts.scheme, address, parts.path, parts.query, parts.fragment))
    except ValueError:
        pass
if os.environ.get("CLOUDSDK_PROXY_ADDRESS") == "localhost":
    os.environ["CLOUDSDK_PROXY_ADDRESS"] = "127.0.0.1"
argv = sys.argv[1:]
if not (isolate_pty and os.isatty(0) and os.isatty(1)):
    os.execvpe(argv[0], argv, os.environ)

# Relay through a fresh pty in a new session. The agent's controlling
# terminal is then this pty, so TIOCSTI cannot inject keystrokes into the
# user's real terminal. Real-terminal fds are close-on-exec (PEP 446).
import fcntl, pty, select, signal, termios, tty
saved = termios.tcgetattr(0)
pid, master = pty.fork()
if pid == 0:
    try:
        os.execvpe(argv[0], argv, os.environ)
    except OSError as error:
        os.write(2, ("srt-agent: cannot start " + argv[0] + ": " + str(error) + "\r\n").encode())
    os._exit(127)
def copy_size(*_):
    try:
        size = fcntl.ioctl(0, termios.TIOCGWINSZ, b"\0" * 8)
        fcntl.ioctl(master, termios.TIOCSWINSZ, size)
        os.kill(pid, signal.SIGWINCH)
    except OSError:
        pass
def forward(signum, _):
    try:
        os.kill(pid, signum)
    except OSError:
        pass
try:
    termios.tcsetattr(master, termios.TCSANOW, saved)
except termios.error:
    pass
copy_size()
signal.signal(signal.SIGWINCH, copy_size)
for signum in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP, signal.SIGQUIT):
    signal.signal(signum, forward)
def write_all(fd, data):
    while data:
        try:
            data = data[os.write(fd, data):]
        except InterruptedError:
            continue
status = None
inputs = [0, master]
tty.setraw(0)
try:
    while True:
        try:
            ready, _, _ = select.select(inputs, [], [], 0.5)
        except InterruptedError:
            continue
        if master in ready:
            try:
                data = os.read(master, 65536)
            except OSError:
                data = b""
            if not data:
                break
            write_all(1, data)
        if 0 in ready:
            try:
                data = os.read(0, 65536)
            except OSError:
                data = b""
            if data:
                write_all(master, data)
            else:
                inputs = [master]
        done, wstatus = os.waitpid(pid, os.WNOHANG | os.WUNTRACED)
        if done and os.WIFSTOPPED(wstatus):
            # There is no outer job control across the new session.
            os.kill(pid, signal.SIGCONT)
        elif done:
            status = wstatus
            # Drain output still buffered in the pty.
            while select.select([master], [], [], 0.05)[0]:
                try:
                    data = os.read(master, 65536)
                except OSError:
                    break
                if not data:
                    break
                write_all(1, data)
            break
finally:
    termios.tcsetattr(0, termios.TCSAFLUSH, saved)
if status is None:
    _, status = os.waitpid(pid, 0)
code = os.waitstatus_to_exitcode(status)
sys.exit(128 - code if code < 0 else code)
'''
CHECK_CODE = r'''
import errno, json, os, pathlib, socket, sys, tempfile
from urllib.parse import urlsplit
policy, launcher, override, base, approvals = map(pathlib.Path, sys.argv[1:6])
messaging_directory = sys.argv[6]
messaging_registry = sys.argv[7]
project = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[8])
path_dirs = [pathlib.Path(p) for p in json.loads(sys.argv[9])]
storage_info = json.loads(sys.argv[10])
srt_probe_domain = sys.argv[11] if len(sys.argv) > 11 else ""
failures = []
warnings = []
for path in ("/etc/hosts", "/private/etc/hosts"):
    try:
        pathlib.Path(path).read_bytes()
        print("PASS: reading resolver file", path)
    except OSError as error:
        print("FAIL: reading resolver file", path, error)
        failures.append(path)
try:
    socket.getaddrinfo("localhost", 0, type=socket.SOCK_STREAM)
    print("PASS: resolving localhost")
except OSError as error:
    print("FAIL: resolving localhost:", error)
    failures.append("localhost resolution")
proxy = os.environ.get("https_proxy") or os.environ.get("HTTPS_PROXY")
if proxy:
    try:
        endpoint = urlsplit(proxy)
        if endpoint.hostname not in ("127.0.0.1", "::1") or endpoint.port is None:
            raise ValueError("expected a numeric loopback proxy endpoint")
        with socket.create_connection((endpoint.hostname, endpoint.port), timeout=3):
            pass
        print("PASS: connecting to the local sandbox proxy")
    except (OSError, ValueError) as error:
        print("FAIL: connecting to the local sandbox proxy:", error)
        failures.append("local proxy")
try:
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="srt-write-check-", dir=os.environ["TMPDIR"]) as directory:
        probe = pathlib.Path(directory) / "probe.txt"
        probe.write_text("temporary write check\n")
        if probe.read_text() != "temporary write check\n":
            raise OSError("temporary file readback mismatch")
    print("PASS: creating directories and files through the agent temporary path")
except OSError as error:
    print("FAIL: agent temporary path is not writable:", error)
    failures.append("agent temporary path")
if messaging_directory:
    probe = pathlib.Path(messaging_directory) / ("check-" + os.urandom(4).hex() + ".sock")
    try:
        with socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM) as server, \
                socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM) as client:
            server.settimeout(3)
            client.settimeout(3)
            server.bind(str(probe))
            os.chmod(probe, 0o600)
            server.listen(1)
            client.connect(str(probe))
            connection, _ = server.accept()
            with connection:
                connection.settimeout(3)
                client.sendall(b"probe")
                if connection.recv(5) != b"probe":
                    raise OSError("Unix messaging socket readback mismatch")
        print("PASS: binding and connecting to a messaging socket")
    except OSError as error:
        print("FAIL: messaging sockets:", error)
        failures.append("messaging sockets")
    finally:
        probe.unlink(missing_ok=True)
if messaging_registry:
    try:
        active_registry = pathlib.Path(os.environ["CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR"]) / "sessions"
        if active_registry.resolve(strict=True) != pathlib.Path(messaging_registry).resolve(strict=True):
            raise OSError("Claude discovery registry does not match the selected messaging scope")
        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=".srt-registry-check-", dir=active_registry) as directory:
            probe = pathlib.Path(directory) / "probe"
            probe.write_text("registry probe")
            if probe.read_text() != "registry probe":
                raise OSError("messaging registry readback mismatch")
        print("PASS: reading and writing the selected Claude discovery registry")
    except OSError as error:
        print("FAIL: Claude messaging registry:", error)
        failures.append("Claude messaging registry")
def denied(label, action, undo=None):
    try:
        result = action()
    except OSError as error:
        if error.errno in (errno.EPERM, errno.EACCES, errno.EROFS):
            print("PASS:", label)
        else:
            print("FAIL:", label, "unexpected error:", error)
            failures.append(label)
    else:
        if undo is not None:
            undo(result)
        print("FAIL:", label, "was allowed")
        failures.append(label)
def remove_probe(result):
    fd, name = result
    os.close(fd)
    os.unlink(name)
denied("creating a file in the policy directory",
       lambda: tempfile.mkstemp(prefix="write-probe-", dir=policy.parent), remove_probe)
denied("writing the approval registry",
       lambda: tempfile.mkstemp(prefix="write-probe-", dir=approvals), remove_probe)
# Unlike opening a mode-0400 file, owner chmod succeeds outside a sandbox.
# This tests sandbox enforcement instead of relying on the read-only mode.
denied("making the generated policy writable", lambda: os.chmod(policy, 0o600),
       lambda _: os.chmod(policy, 0o400))
denied("reading the launcher", lambda: os.open(launcher, os.O_RDONLY), os.close)
for label, path in (("writing the launcher", launcher),
                    ("writing the project override", override),
                    ("writing the base policy", base)):
    denied(label, lambda path=path: os.open(path, os.O_WRONLY), os.close)
# Host-side Git executes hooks and config-defined commands. Both must stay
# out of reach, including by renaming the whole .git directory away.
git = project / ".git"
if git.is_dir():
    denied("creating a Git hook",
           lambda: tempfile.mkstemp(prefix="hook-probe-", dir=git / "hooks") if (git / "hooks").is_dir()
           else os.mkdir(git / "hooks"),
           lambda result: remove_probe(result) if isinstance(result, tuple) else os.rmdir(git / "hooks"))
    if (git / "config").exists():
        denied("writing .git/config", lambda: os.open(git / "config", os.O_WRONLY), os.close)
    moved = project / (".git-srt-check-" + os.urandom(4).hex())
    denied("renaming the .git directory", lambda: os.rename(git, moved),
           lambda _: os.rename(moved, git))
# Files that host tools load or execute from the project.
for name in (".envrc", ".env"):
    target = project / name
    if target.exists() or target.is_symlink():
        denied("writing " + name, lambda target=target: os.open(target, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW), os.close)
    else:
        denied("creating " + name, lambda target=target: os.open(target, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL, 0o600),
               lambda fd, target=target: (os.close(fd), os.unlink(target)))
vscode = project / ".vscode"
if vscode.is_dir():
    denied("creating a file in .vscode",
           lambda: tempfile.mkstemp(prefix="vscode-probe-", dir=vscode), remove_probe)
else:
    denied("creating .vscode", lambda: os.mkdir(vscode), lambda _: os.rmdir(vscode))
# A new file in any PATH directory could shadow a command.
for directory in path_dirs:
    try:
        probe_directory = directory.is_dir()
    except OSError:
        # Unreadable inside the sandbox (e.g. a host PATH entry under the
        # denied home). Python 3.9 raises here; still prove it is unwritable.
        probe_directory = True
    if probe_directory:
        denied("creating a file in PATH directory " + str(directory),
               lambda directory=directory: tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=".path-probe-", dir=directory), remove_probe)
# The venv interpreter must run, and its config must stay host-only.
venv = os.environ.get("VIRTUAL_ENV")
if venv:
    import shutil, subprocess
    python = shutil.which("python") or shutil.which("python3")
    try:
        if python is None:
            raise OSError("no python on the agent PATH")
        result = subprocess.run([python, "-c", "import sys; print(sys.prefix)"], stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                                stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True, timeout=30)
        if result.returncode != 0:
            raise OSError(result.stderr.strip() or "exit status " + str(result.returncode))
        if pathlib.Path(result.stdout.strip()).resolve() != pathlib.Path(venv).resolve():
            raise OSError("python on PATH uses prefix " + result.stdout.strip())
        print("PASS: python on PATH runs from VIRTUAL_ENV", venv)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as error:
        print("FAIL: virtualenv python:", error)
        failures.append("virtualenv python")
    venv_config = pathlib.Path(venv) / "pyvenv.cfg"
    denied("writing the virtualenv pyvenv.cfg", lambda: os.open(venv_config, os.O_WRONLY), os.close)
# srt must use only the generated policy: a domain allowed solely in srt's
# own ~/.srt-settings.json must be refused by the sandbox proxy.
if srt_probe_domain and proxy:
    import base64
    from urllib.parse import unquote
    endpoint = urlsplit(proxy)
    request = "CONNECT " + srt_probe_domain + ":443 HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: " + srt_probe_domain + ":443\r\n"
    if endpoint.username:
        token = base64.b64encode((unquote(endpoint.username) + ":" + unquote(endpoint.password or "")).encode()).decode()
        request += "Proxy-Authorization: Basic " + token + "\r\n"
    # Only an explicit allowlist refusal from srt's proxy counts as PASS.
    # An unreachable proxy, a timeout or any other answer proves nothing.
    try:
        with socket.create_connection((endpoint.hostname, endpoint.port), timeout=10) as conn:
            conn.sendall((request + "\r\n").encode())
            head = b""
            # A refusal is short and the proxy closes after it; an accepted
            # tunnel stays open, so stop once headers have arrived and the
            # line goes quiet.
            while len(head) < 8192:
                try:
                    chunk = conn.recv(1024)
                except socket.timeout:
                    if b"\r\n\r\n" in head:
                        break
                    raise
                if not chunk:
                    break
                head += chunk
                if b"\r\n\r\n" in head:
                    conn.settimeout(2)
        header_block, _, body = head.partition(b"\r\n\r\n")
        lines = header_block.decode("latin-1", "replace").split("\r\n")
        body = body.decode("latin-1", "replace").lower()
        status, headers = lines[0].strip(), [line.lower() for line in lines[1:]]
        code = status.split(" ")[1] if len(status.split(" ")) > 1 else ""
        if code == "200":
            print("FAIL: srt allowed", srt_probe_domain, "which only ~/.srt-settings.json allows: srt merges that file")
            failures.append("srt merges ~/.srt-settings.json")
        elif code == "403" and (any(h.startswith("x-proxy-error:") and "blocked" in h for h in headers)
                                or "blocked by network allowlist" in body):
            print("PASS: srt uses only the generated policy (" + srt_probe_domain + " refused by the allowlist)")
        else:
            print("INCONCLUSIVE: srt independence:", srt_probe_domain, "got", repr(status or "no answer"),
                  "instead of the proxy's allowlist refusal")
            warnings.append("srt independence check inconclusive (unexpected proxy answer)")
    except OSError as error:
        print("INCONCLUSIVE: srt independence: could not query the sandbox proxy (" + str(error) + ")")
        warnings.append("srt independence check inconclusive (proxy unreachable)")
elif srt_probe_domain:
    print("INCONCLUSIVE: srt independence: no sandbox proxy in the environment")
    warnings.append("srt independence check inconclusive (no proxy)")
else:
    print("SKIP: srt independence (no domain allowed only in ~/.srt-settings.json to probe; add one there to test)")
# Agent storage: launcher-owned parts, other agents and other projects.
identity = pathlib.Path(storage_info["identity"])
host_temp = pathlib.Path(storage_info["host_temp"])
denied("creating a file in srt's host-side temp folder",
       lambda: os.open(host_temp / ("check-" + os.urandom(4).hex()), os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL, 0o600), os.close)
denied("listing srt's host-side temp folder", lambda: os.listdir(host_temp))
shared_home = storage_info.get("shared_home")
if shared_home and os.path.isdir(shared_home):
    denied("reading the shared agent home (this project uses isolated homes)", lambda: os.listdir(shared_home))
denied("reading the agent storage identity record", lambda: open(identity, "rb").read())
denied("writing the agent storage identity record", lambda: os.open(identity, os.O_WRONLY), os.close)
home = pathlib.Path(os.environ["HOME"])
moved_home = home.with_name(home.name + ".moved-check")
denied("replacing this agent's home folder", lambda: os.rename(home, moved_home),
       lambda _: os.rename(moved_home, home))
# Existence comes from the launcher (host side): inside the sandbox a
# denied lookup and a missing folder can look alike.
for label, folder in (("other projects' agent storage", storage_info["storage_base"]),
                      ("other projects' caches", storage_info["cache_base"])):
    if folder:
        denied("listing " + label, lambda folder=folder: os.listdir(folder))
    else:
        print("SKIP: listing " + label + " (not created yet)")
for item in storage_info["siblings"]:
    sibling, exists = pathlib.Path(item["path"]), item["exists"]
    probe = sibling / ("check-" + os.urandom(4).hex())
    if exists:
        denied("reading agent " + sibling.name + "'s storage", lambda sibling=sibling: os.listdir(sibling))
        denied("writing into agent " + sibling.name + "'s storage",
               lambda probe=probe: os.open(probe, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL, 0o600),
               lambda fd, probe=probe: (os.close(fd), os.unlink(probe)))
    else:
        denied("creating agent " + sibling.name + "'s storage", lambda sibling=sibling: os.mkdir(sibling),
               lambda _, sibling=sibling: os.rmdir(sibling))
# srt compatibility, not a security property: srt's built-in blocks on
# .git/hooks, .vscode and shell rc files have covered only the project.
# Tests that create repositories in TMPDIR rely on that.
compat = pathlib.Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="srt-compat-", dir=os.environ["TMPDIR"]))
try:
    (compat / ".git/hooks").mkdir(parents=True)
    (compat / ".git/hooks/pre-commit").write_text("probe")
    (compat / ".vscode").mkdir()
    (compat / ".vscode/settings.json").write_text("{}")
    (compat / ".bashrc").write_text("probe")
    print("PASS: Git hooks, .vscode and .bashrc can be created in the agent temp folder (srt compatibility)")
except OSError as error:
    print("WARN: srt now blocks Git hooks, .vscode or .bashrc outside the project too:", error)
    warnings.append("srt blocks Git hooks/.vscode/.bashrc in the agent temp folder: tests that create "
                    "repositories or rc files in TMPDIR will fail")
finally:
    import shutil as _shutil
    _shutil.rmtree(compat, ignore_errors=True)
runtime = os.environ.get("XDG_RUNTIME_DIR")
if runtime:
    sock_path = pathlib.Path(runtime) / ("srt-check-" + os.urandom(12).hex() + ".sock")
    try:
        with socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM) as server:
            server.bind(str(sock_path))
        print("PASS: Unix socket path fits macOS limits (" + str(len(str(sock_path))) + " bytes)")
    except OSError as error:
        print("FAIL: Unix socket in XDG_RUNTIME_DIR (" + str(len(str(sock_path))) + " bytes):", error)
        failures.append("socket path length")
    finally:
        sock_path.unlink(missing_ok=True)
# The shared tools venv must run as a venv and stay read-only.
import shutil, subprocess
toolpy = shutil.which("toolpy")
if toolpy:
    try:
        result = subprocess.run([toolpy, "-c", "import sys; print(sys.prefix != sys.base_prefix); print(sys.prefix)"],
                                stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True, timeout=30)
        lines = result.stdout.split("\n")
        if result.returncode != 0 or lines[0] != "True":
            raise OSError(result.stderr.strip() or "toolpy did not start inside its venv")
        print("PASS: toolpy runs the shared tools venv", lines[1])
        denied("writing into the shared tools venv",
               lambda: tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=".tools-probe-", dir=lines[1]), remove_probe)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as error:
        print("FAIL: toolpy:", error)
        failures.append("toolpy")
# TIOCSTI pushes bytes into a terminal's input queue. Interactive launches
# isolate the agent on its own pty; this reports whether srt also blocks it.
try:
    import fcntl, termios
    request = getattr(termios, "TIOCSTI", 0x80017472)
    with open("/dev/tty", "rb", buffering=0) as terminal:
        fcntl.ioctl(terminal, request, b"\x15")
    print("WARN: TIOCSTI to the launch terminal is not blocked by srt; keep pty isolation on")
    warnings.append("TIOCSTI is not blocked by srt: keep pty isolation on")
except OSError as error:
    if error.errno == errno.ENXIO:
        print("SKIP: no controlling terminal for the TIOCSTI test")
    else:
        print("PASS: TIOCSTI to the launch terminal is blocked")
print()
if failures:
    print("SUMMARY: " + str(len(failures)) + " check(s) FAILED: " + ", ".join(failures))
else:
    print("SUMMARY: all security checks passed")
for warning in warnings:
    print("SUMMARY WARNING: " + warning)
raise SystemExit(1 if failures else 0)
'''


def fail(message):
    raise RuntimeError(message)


def account_home():
    return Path(pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid()).pw_dir).resolve()


def home_directories():
    return {Path.home().resolve(), account_home()}


def project_settings_path(project):
    # The global config lives in ~/.config/srt-agent, so even a home-folder
    # project no longer collides with it.
    return project / PROJECT_SETTINGS


def mandatory_denials():
    root = Path("/root")
    launcher = Path(__file__).absolute()
    return list(dict.fromkeys((root, root.resolve(), launcher, launcher.resolve())))


def host_exec_protections(project):
    # Host-side git runs hooks and commands named in config (core.fsmonitor,
    # core.hooksPath, filters, aliases...). Deny them even before .git exists.
    git = project / ".git"
    paths = [git / "config", git / "config.worktree", git / "hooks", git / "info" / "attributes"]
    if git.is_file() or not git.exists():
        # A gitlink file can redirect the repository elsewhere.
        paths.append(git)
    # direnv sources .envrc in your host shell on cd (once allowed, it stays
    # allowed only for unchanged content, but a new file is one keystroke
    # from running). Deny it whether or not it exists yet.
    paths.append(project / ".envrc")
    # Loaded by dotenv libraries, docker compose and many dev servers.
    paths.append(project / ".env")
    # VS Code runs tasks.json/launch.json and executables named in
    # settings.json (formatters, linters, terminal profiles, interpreters).
    paths.append(project / ".vscode")
    return paths


def path_protections(project, agent_path):
    # Write-deny every PATH directory, host and agent, under both its lexical
    # and resolved spelling, so nothing new can shadow or replace a command.
    entries = os.environ.get("PATH", "").split(os.pathsep) + list(agent_path)
    result = []
    for entry in entries:
        path = Path(entry or ".")
        if not path.is_absolute():
            path = project / path
        for spelled in dict.fromkeys((Path(os.path.normpath(path)), path.resolve())):
            if project.is_relative_to(spelled):
                fail("PATH entry " + json.dumps(entry, ensure_ascii=True) + " is the project root or an ancestor; "
                     "write-denying it would block every project write. Remove it from PATH")
            result.append(spelled)
    return list(dict.fromkeys(result))


def reject_protected_grant(path):
    if any(path.is_relative_to(protected) for protected in mandatory_denials()):
        fail("Project grant targets a permanently protected path: " + str(path))


def approval_directory(create=False):
    home = account_home()
    directory = home / ".local/state/srt-agent/approvals"
    current = home
    for part in directory.relative_to(home).parts:
        current = current / part
        if current.is_symlink():
            fail("Approval storage must not contain symlinks: " + str(current))
    if create:
        directory.mkdir(parents=True, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    if directory.exists():
        if not directory.is_dir() or directory.stat().st_uid != os.getuid():
            fail("Approval storage must be a directory owned by you")
        if create:
            directory.chmod(0o700)
    return directory


def parse_jsonc(raw, label, comments=True):
    # JSON plus // and /* */ comments and trailing commas, nothing else.
    # Pass 1 removes comments with a character tokenizer that tracks strings
    # and escapes (so "https://..." is never touched), replacing each comment
    # with the same number of newlines to keep error line numbers right.
    # Pass 2 drops a comma only when the next non-space character outside a
    # string closes an object or array. The result must then be strict JSON:
    # duplicate keys, NaN/Infinity and stray characters are errors, never
    # silently resolved.
    try:
        text = raw.decode("utf-8")
    except UnicodeDecodeError as error:
        fail(label + " is not valid UTF-8: " + str(error))
    if text.startswith("\ufeff"):
        text = text[1:]
    def unique_pairs(pairs):
        obj = {}
        for key, value in pairs:
            if key in obj:
                raise ValueError("duplicate key " + json.dumps(key, ensure_ascii=True))
            obj[key] = value
        return obj

    def no_constants(name):
        raise ValueError("non-standard number " + name)

    def decode(source):
        try:
            return json.loads(source, object_pairs_hook=unique_pairs, parse_constant=no_constants)
        except ValueError as error:
            fail(label + ": " + str(error))

    if not comments:  # strict JSON (srt's own files): same duplicate/NaN checks
        return decode(text)

    def where(index):
        return label + ": line " + str(text.count("\n", 0, index) + 1)

    out = []
    i, n, string_start = 0, len(text), None
    while i < n:
        c = text[i]
        if string_start is not None:
            out.append(c)
            if c == "\\":
                if i + 1 >= n:
                    fail(where(i) + ": unterminated string")
                out.append(text[i + 1])
                i += 2
                continue
            if c == '"':
                string_start = None
            elif c == "\n":
                fail(where(i) + ": line break inside a string")
            i += 1
        elif c == '"':
            string_start = i
            out.append(c)
            i += 1
        elif text.startswith("//", i):
            end = text.find("\n", i)
            end = n if end < 0 else end  # keep the newline itself
            out.append(" " * (end - i))  # same width: error columns stay exact
            i = end
        elif text.startswith("/*", i):
            end = text.find("*/", i + 2)
            if end < 0:
                fail(where(i) + ": unterminated /* comment")
            # Same shape: newlines kept, everything else blanked, so error
            # lines and columns point at the real text.
            out.append("".join(ch if ch == "\n" else " " for ch in text[i:end + 2]))
            i = end + 2
        elif c == "/":
            fail(where(i) + ": unexpected '/' outside a string or comment")
        else:
            out.append(c)
            i += 1
    if string_start is not None:
        fail(where(string_start) + ": unterminated string")
    stripped = "".join(out)
    result = []
    i, n, in_string, last = 0, len(stripped), False, ""
    while i < n:
        c = stripped[i]
        if in_string:
            result.append(c)
            if c == "\\":
                result.append(stripped[i + 1])
                i += 2
                continue
            if c == '"':
                in_string = False
                last = '"'
        elif c == '"':
            in_string = True
            result.append(c)
        elif c == ",":
            j = i + 1
            while j < n and stripped[j] in " \t\r\n":
                j += 1
            if j >= n or stripped[j] not in "}]" or last in ("", "[", "{", ",", ":"):
                result.append(c)  # a separator, or a stray comma for json to reject
                last = ","
            else:
                result.append(" ")  # a trailing comma after a value: blanked, keeping columns
        else:
            result.append(c)
            if c not in " \t\r\n":
                last = c
        i += 1

    return decode("".join(result))


def project_key(project):
    return hashlib.sha256(os.fsencode(str(project))).hexdigest()


def approval_path(project):
    return approval_directory() / (project_key(project) + ".json")


def read_regular(path):
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as handle:
        metadata = os.fstat(handle.fileno())
        if not stat.S_ISREG(metadata.st_mode) or metadata.st_uid != os.getuid():
            fail("Settings/approval must be a regular file owned by you: " + str(path))
        raw = handle.read(1024 * 1024 + 1)
        if len(raw) > 1024 * 1024:
            fail("Settings/approval exceeds 1 MiB: " + str(path))
        return raw


def settings_digest(data):
    # Approvals bind the parsed settings, not the bytes: editing a comment or
    # reformatting does not ask again; any change in meaning does.
    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(data, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=True, separators=(",", ":"))
                          .encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()


def project_identity(project, path, raw, grants, base_policy):
    return {
        "format": TRUST_FORMAT,
        "project": str(project),
        "config_path": str(path),
        "content_sha256": settings_digest(parse_jsonc(raw, str(path))),
        # Include resolved targets: retargeting a symlink must require approval
        # even when the JSON bytes have not changed.
        "permissions_sha256": hashlib.sha256(
            json.dumps(grants, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=True).encode("utf-8")
        ).hexdigest(),
        "base_policy": {key: value for key, value in base_policy.items() if key != "configuration"},
    }


def effective_switches(base_policy, grants):
    switches = dict(base_policy.get("switches", {}))
    switches.update(grants.get("switches", {}))
    return switches


LOOSENING = (
    # (summary key, direction, question)
    ("allowedDomains", "added", "new network domains"),
    ("deniedDomains", "removed", "removed domain blocks"),
    ("allowUnixSockets", "added", "new Unix sockets (host services outside the sandbox)"),
    ("allowMachLookup", "added", "new Mach services (host services outside the sandbox)"),
    ("allowRead", "added", "new read access"),
    ("allowWrite", "added", "new write access"),
    ("denyRead", "removed", "removed read blocks"),
    ("denyWrite", "removed", "removed write blocks"),
    ("switches", "added", "sandbox switches turned on"),
)


def approval_summary(base_policy, grants):
    # What the agents end up with, by category, for comparing approvals.
    # Agent-specific additions come from the global config and are covered
    # by its own diff.
    def text(entry):
        return entry["path"] if isinstance(entry, dict) else entry
    network = base_policy["effective_configuration"].get("network", {})
    summary = {}
    for key in ("allowedDomains", "deniedDomains", "allowUnixSockets", "allowMachLookup"):
        summary[key] = sorted(set(network.get(key, []) or []) | set(grants.get(key, []) or []))
    for key in ("allowRead", "allowWrite", "denyRead", "denyWrite"):
        summary[key] = sorted({text(e) for e in base_policy["filesystem"].get(key, [])}
                              | {text(e) for e in grants.get(key, [])})
    summary["switches"] = sorted(k for k, v in effective_switches(base_policy, grants).items() if v)
    return summary


def loosening_changes(old, new, project=None):
    # Access inside the project itself is the expected workspace, not a
    # loosening worth its own question; it still shows in the full diff.
    changes = []
    for key, direction, question in LOOSENING:
        before, after = set(old.get(key, [])), set(new.get(key, []))
        items = sorted(after - before) if direction == "added" else sorted(before - after)
        if project is not None and key in ("allowRead", "allowWrite"):
            items = [i for i in items if not Path(i).is_relative_to(project)]
        if items:
            changes.append((key, question, items))
    return changes


def risky_ipc(base_policy, grants):
    network = base_policy["effective_configuration"].get("network", {})
    sockets = list(network.get("allowUnixSockets", []) or []) + grants["allowUnixSockets"]
    warnings = [s for s in sockets if isinstance(s, str) and any(h in s.lower() for h in RISKY_SOCKET_HINTS)]
    return warnings


def require_approval(project, path, raw, data, grants, base_policy, allow_home=False, venv=None, mode="env"):
    if os.environ.get("SANDBOX_RUNTIME") == "1":
        fail("Project approvals must be managed outside a running sandbox")
    record_path = approval_path(project)
    try:
        previous = json.loads(read_regular(record_path))
        if not isinstance(previous, dict):
            fail("Invalid approval record: " + str(record_path))
    except FileNotFoundError:
        previous = {}
    identity = project_identity(project, path, raw, grants, base_policy)
    project_ok = previous.get("identity") == identity
    # Venv approvals are kept only alongside the project approval they were
    # granted under; re-approving changed settings starts the list afresh.
    approved_venvs = previous.get("virtual_envs", []) if project_ok else []
    if not isinstance(approved_venvs, list):
        fail("Invalid approval record: " + str(record_path))
    venv_ok = venv is None or venv in approved_venvs
    if project_ok and venv_ok:
        return
    if not sys.stdin.isatty() or not sys.stderr.isatty():
        fail("Project settings or virtualenv need approval; run srt-agent project approve "
             "in an interactive terminal (with the same venv options)")
    # Use a real terminal rather than accepting piped yes/input. JSON escaping
    # prevents control characters in project settings from spoofing the prompt.
    # A buffered r+ stream uses BufferedRandom, which requires seek support.
    # Real terminals are not seekable; keep independent input/output handles.
    with open("/dev/tty", "r", encoding="utf-8") as terminal_input, \
            open("/dev/tty", "w", encoding="utf-8", buffering=1) as terminal:
        # Discard anything queued on the terminal before the prompt, such as
        # keystrokes injected by an earlier process, so only new input counts.
        try:
            import termios
            termios.tcflush(terminal_input.fileno(), termios.TCIFLUSH)
        except (ImportError, OSError):
            pass
        if not project_ok:
            terminal.write("\nsrt-agent: global or project settings are new or modified.\n")
            terminal.write("Global file: " + json.dumps(base_policy["path"], ensure_ascii=True) + "\n")
            old_base = (json.dumps(previous.get("base_configuration", {}), indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=True) + "\n").splitlines(True)
            new_base = (json.dumps(base_policy["configuration"], indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=True) + "\n").splitlines(True)
            terminal.write("\n" + "".join(difflib.unified_diff(old_base, new_base, fromfile="approved global", tofile="requested global")) + "\n")
            terminal.write("Global filesystem permissions after project removals:\n" + json.dumps(base_policy["filesystem"], indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=True) + "\n")
            terminal.write("File: " + json.dumps(str(path), ensure_ascii=True) + "\n")
            old = (json.dumps(previous.get("configuration", {}), indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=True) + "\n").splitlines(True)
            new = (json.dumps(data, indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=True) + "\n").splitlines(True)
            terminal.write("\n" + "".join(difflib.unified_diff(old, new, fromfile="approved", tofile="requested")) + "\n")
            terminal.write("Inherited entries to remove (exact matches):\n" + json.dumps(grants["remove"], indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=True) + "\n")
            terminal.write("Resolved project permissions:\n" + json.dumps(grants, indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=True) + "\n")
            if base_policy.get("tools"):
                terminal.write("Shared tools venv (read-only, on every agent PATH, run as toolpy):\n"
                               + json.dumps(base_policy["tools"], indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=True) + "\n")
            if grants["allowUnixSockets"] or grants["allowMachLookup"]:
                terminal.write("Host IPC services may act outside the sandbox. Review each service.\n")
            for entry in risky_ipc(base_policy, grants):
                terminal.write("WARNING: " + json.dumps(entry, ensure_ascii=True)
                               + " can usually run commands or use credentials as you, outside the sandbox.\n")
        if not project_ok:
            # Ask separately for each kind of loosening, against what was
            # last approved (or, the first time, against the global baseline),
            # so a widened permission cannot hide inside a long diff.
            empty = {"allowUnixSockets": [], "allowMachLookup": [], "remove": {}}
            old_summary = previous.get("summary") if isinstance(previous.get("summary"), dict) else \
                approval_summary(base_policy, {**empty, "allowRead": [], "allowWrite": [], "denyRead": [], "denyWrite": []})
            for key, question, items in loosening_changes(old_summary, approval_summary(base_policy, grants), project):
                terminal.write("\nLOOSENS SECURITY: " + question + ":\n")
                for item in items:
                    note = (" - " + SWITCHES[item][1]) if key == "switches" else ""
                    if key == "allowUnixSockets" and any(h in item.lower() for h in RISKY_SOCKET_HINTS):
                        note = " - can usually run commands or use credentials as you"
                    terminal.write("    " + json.dumps(item, ensure_ascii=True) + note + "\n")
                terminal.write("Accept " + ("this" if len(items) == 1 else "these " + str(len(items))) + "? [y/N] ")
                terminal.flush()
                if terminal_input.readline().strip().lower() not in ("y", "yes"):
                    fail("Not approved (" + question + "); nothing was launched")
        if not venv_ok:
            terminal.write("\nsrt-agent: this virtualenv is not yet approved for this project.\n")
            terminal.write("Its bin goes first on the agent PATH and these paths become readable:\n"
                           + json.dumps(venv, indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=True) + "\n")
        terminal.write("Approve these exact settings for this project? [y/N] ")
        terminal.flush()
        accepted = terminal_input.readline().strip().lower() in ("y", "yes")
    if not accepted:
        fail("Project settings were not approved; nothing was launched")
    # Parse once, approve that snapshot, and generate from it. Refuse changes
    # made during review rather than approving one file and reading another.
    _, current_grants, _, current_raw = project_permissions(project, base_policy["path"], allow_home=allow_home)
    if current_raw != raw or current_grants != grants:
        fail("Project settings or resolved paths changed during review; review again")
    if load_base_policy(project, base_policy["path"], allow_home=allow_home, removals=grants["remove"]) != base_policy:
        fail("Global settings or resolved paths changed during review; review again")
    if venv is not None and detect_virtualenv(project, mode) != venv:
        fail("Virtualenv or its resolved paths changed during review; review again")
    if not venv_ok:
        approved_venvs = approved_venvs + [venv]
    directory = approval_directory(create=True)
    fd, temporary = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=".approval-", dir=directory)
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as handle:
            json.dump({"identity": identity, "configuration": data,
                       "base_configuration": base_policy["configuration"],
                       "summary": approval_summary(base_policy, grants),
                       "virtual_envs": approved_venvs}, handle, indent=2, ensure_ascii=True)
            handle.write("\n")
        os.replace(temporary, record_path)
    finally:
        if os.path.exists(temporary):
            os.unlink(temporary)


def revoke_approval(project):
    if os.environ.get("SANDBOX_RUNTIME") == "1":
        fail("Project approvals must be managed outside a running sandbox")
    approval_path(project).unlink(missing_ok=True)
    print("Revoked project approval:", project)


def find_binary(binary, override_name, project=None):
    override = os.environ.get("SRT_AGENT_" + override_name.upper().replace("-", "_"))
    if override:
        candidate = Path(override).expanduser().absolute()
        if not candidate.is_file() or not os.access(candidate, os.X_OK):
            fail("Not an executable: " + str(candidate))
        return str(candidate)
    # Native Homebrew installs are found even when the host PATH is minimal.
    for directory in ("/opt/homebrew/bin", "/usr/local/bin"):
        candidate = Path(directory) / binary
        if candidate.is_file() and os.access(candidate, os.X_OK):
            return str(candidate)
    found = shutil.which(binary, path=host_path(project))
    if found:
        return str(Path(found).absolute())
    fail("Cannot find " + binary + "; set SRT_AGENT_" + override_name.upper().replace("-", "_"))


def host_path(project=None):
    # Only absolute directories, never the project or the working directory:
    # srt and the executables it runs (e.g. node via env) resolve through this.
    default = "/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin"
    entries = []
    for entry in os.environ.get("PATH", default).split(os.pathsep):
        if not entry or not os.path.isabs(entry):
            continue
        if project is not None:
            try:
                if Path(entry).resolve().is_relative_to(project):
                    continue
            except OSError:
                continue
        entries.append(entry)
    return os.pathsep.join(dict.fromkeys(entries)) or default


def find_git_root(start):
    # Equivalent to git rev-parse --show-toplevel for ordinary repositories,
    # worktrees and submodules, without executing git or reading its config
    # from an agent-writable directory.
    for candidate in (start, *start.parents):
        if os.path.lexists(candidate / ".git"):
            return candidate
    return None


def project_root(explicit, allow_home=False):
    homes = home_directories()
    cwd = Path.cwd().resolve()
    root_denials = {Path("/root"), Path("/root").resolve()}
    if cwd == Path("/") or any(cwd.is_relative_to(root) for root in root_denials):
        fail("Refusing to run from / or /root")
    if cwd in homes and not allow_home:
        fail("Running from home requires --allow-home")
    if explicit:
        root = Path(explicit).expanduser().resolve(strict=True)
    else:
        root = find_git_root(cwd) or cwd
    if not root.is_dir() or root == Path("/") or any(root.is_relative_to(denied) for denied in root_denials):
        fail("Refusing / or /root as the project root")
    if root in homes and not allow_home:
        fail("Using home as the project root requires --allow-home")
    trust_root = approval_directory().parent
    if root.is_relative_to(trust_root) or (trust_root.is_relative_to(root) and not (root in homes and allow_home)):
        fail("Project must not overlap the trusted approval store")
    return root


def init_project(project, settings=None, extends=()):
    path = project_settings_path(project)
    references = []
    for value in extends:
        for name in value.split(","):
            name = name.strip()
            if name:
                references.append(name)
    references = list(dict.fromkeys(references))
    if references:
        # Check against the global groups now, not first at launch.
        groups = global_groups(project, settings)
        for reference in references:
            if not GROUP_NAME.fullmatch(reference):
                fail("Invalid group name: " + reference)
            if reference not in groups:
                fail("Unknown group " + reference + "; defined groups: " + (", ".join(sorted(groups)) or "none"))
    override = ({"extends": references} if references else {})
    override["filesystem"] = {"allowRead": ["."], "allowWrite": ["."]}
    # Exclusive create refuses existing files and symlinks. No source settings,
    # shell profiles, generated policies or agent state are changed here.
    body = json.dumps(override, indent=2)
    with path.open("x") as handle:
        handle.write("// srt-agent project settings (JSON with comments and trailing commas).\n"
                     "// Agents cannot change this file; any change in meaning needs your approval.\n"
                     + body + "\n")
    print("Created project override:", path)
    if references:
        print("Extends:", ", ".join(references))


def project_permissions(project, base_settings, allow_home=False):
    if project in home_directories() and not allow_home:
        fail("Home project settings require --allow-home")
    path = project_settings_path(project)
    if path.is_symlink():
        fail("Project override must not be a symlink: " + str(path))
    if not path.is_file():
        fail("No project override at " + str(path) + "; run srt-agent project init to opt in")
    if base_settings is not None and path.resolve() == Path(base_settings).expanduser().resolve():
        fail("Base and project settings must be different files")
    raw = read_regular(path)
    data = parse_jsonc(raw, str(path))  # shown in the approval diff as written
    flat = flat_layer(data, str(path), PROJECT_LAUNCHER_KEYS, ("remove", "extends"))
    effective = flat
    group_names = []
    group_domains = []
    group_files_used = {}
    if "extends" in flat:
        # Global groups first, in the order listed, then this file last.
        extends = flat["extends"]
        if not isinstance(extends, list) or any(
                not isinstance(e, str) or not GROUP_NAME.fullmatch(e) for e in extends):
            fail('Project extends must be an array of group names like "lang/rust"')
        if base_settings is None:
            fail("Project extends needs the global settings file that defines its groups")
        groups, group_sources = global_groups(project, base_settings, with_sources=True)
        layers = []
        for reference in expand_groups(extends, groups, group_directory(project, base_settings)):
            if reference in group_sources:
                # Bound to THIS project's approval (via permissions) and shown
                # in its approval diff; projects not using it are unaffected.
                source, parsed = group_sources[reference]
                group_files_used[reference] = source
                data = {**data, "(group file " + source["path"] + ")": parsed}
            group = copy.deepcopy(groups[reference])
            group.pop("extends", None)
            layers.append(group)
            group_names.append(reference)
        own = {key: value for key, value in flat.items() if key != "extends"}
        effective = merge_layers(layers + [own])
    if "filesystem" not in effective:
        fail("Project override (with its groups) must provide a filesystem object")
    filesystem = effective["filesystem"]
    allowed = REMOVABLE_LISTS["filesystem"]
    if not isinstance(filesystem, dict) or set(filesystem) - set(allowed):
        fail("Project filesystem overrides support allowRead, allowWrite, denyRead and denyWrite only")
    permissions = {"remove": validate_removals(effective.get("remove", {}))}
    network = effective.get("network", {})
    if not isinstance(network, dict):
        fail("Project network must be an object")
    for name in ("allowedDomains", "deniedDomains"):
        if network.get(name):
            permissions[name] = validate_domains(network[name], "Project network." + name)
    if effective.get("switches"):
        permissions["switches"] = dict(effective["switches"])
    if "extends" in flat:
        # Recorded only when used, so existing approvals stay valid.
        permissions["groups"] = group_names
        permissions.setdefault("allowedDomains", [])
        if group_files_used:
            permissions["group_files"] = group_files_used
    for name in allowed:
        entries = filesystem.get(name, [])
        if not isinstance(entries, list):
            fail("Project filesystem." + name + " must be an array")
        paths = []
        for entry in entries:
            if not isinstance(entry, str) or not entry:
                fail("Project override paths must be nonempty strings")
            resolved = resolve_project_path(project, entry)
            if name.startswith("allow"):
                reject_protected_grant(resolved)
            if name == "allowRead":
                if account_home().is_relative_to(resolved) and not (resolved == account_home() and allow_home):
                    fail("Root/ancestor read grants are forbidden; whole-home reads require --allow-home: " + entry)
                # An explicit /etc grant must retain the /etc symlink name,
                # not just its /private/etc target. Approve both spellings;
                # the target remains part of the approval digest. Avoid
                # inventing a lexical spelling for paths containing '..'.
                spelled = resolve_project_path(project, entry, canonical=False)
                if ".." not in spelled.parts and spelled != resolved:
                    reject_protected_grant(spelled)
                    paths.append(literal(spelled))
            elif name == "allowWrite" and not resolved.is_relative_to(project):
                fail("Project override path escapes this project: " + entry)
            elif name.startswith("deny"):
                spelled = resolve_project_path(project, entry, canonical=False)
                if ".." not in spelled.parts:
                    paths.append(literal(spelled))
            paths.append(literal(resolved))
        permissions[name] = unique_entries(paths)
    if set(network) - set(REMOVABLE_LISTS["network"]):
        fail("Project network supports " + ", ".join(REMOVABLE_LISTS["network"])
             + ", allowLocalBinding and allowAllUnixSockets")
    for name in ("allowUnixSockets", "allowMachLookup"):
        values = network.get(name, [])
        if not isinstance(values, list) or any(not isinstance(v, str) or not v for v in values):
            fail("Project network." + name + " must be an array of nonempty strings")
        if name == "allowUnixSockets":
            resolved_values = []
            for value in values:
                resolved = resolve_project_path(project, value)
                reject_protected_grant(resolved)
                if resolved.is_dir() or account_home().is_relative_to(resolved):
                    fail("Allow an individual Unix socket path, not a directory: " + value)
                resolved_values.append(str(resolved))
            permissions[name] = resolved_values
        else:
            if any("*" in v or any(ord(c) < 33 or ord(c) > 126 for c in v) for v in values):
                fail("Mach lookups must name exact services without wildcards or whitespace")
            permissions[name] = values
    # Per-project launcher additions. Like the rest of this file they are
    # write-denied to agents and bound to the approval, with resolved
    # targets included so retargeting a symlink asks again.
    # Recorded only when present, so existing approvals stay valid.
    if "srtAgent" not in effective:
        return path, permissions, data, raw
    launcher = effective["srtAgent"]
    if "agentHome" in launcher:
        # Credential access: bound to the approval like any other grant.
        permissions["agentHome"] = validate_agent_home(launcher["agentHome"], "Project agentHome")
    permissions["launcher"] = {
        "path": validate_path_entries(launcher.get("path", []), "Project path"),
        "setEnv": validate_set_env(launcher.get("setEnv", {}), "Project setEnv"),
        "resolved_path": [str(resolve_project_path(project, e)) for e in launcher.get("path", [])],
        # What the agent actually receives: ~/ is your account home, never
        # the private HOME inside the sandbox.
        "resolved_setEnv": {name: expand_env_value(value, project) for name, value in launcher.get("setEnv", {}).items()},
    }
    return path, permissions, data, raw


def resolve_project_path(project, entry, canonical=True):
    if entry == "~":
        path = account_home()
    elif entry.startswith("~/"):
        path = account_home() / entry[2:]
    elif entry.startswith("~"):
        fail("Only ~/ for your account home is supported")
    else:
        path = Path(entry)
        if not path.is_absolute():
            path = project / path
    return path.resolve() if canonical else path.absolute()


def read_small_text(path, limit, label):
    # Venv files may be agent-written: refuse FIFOs/devices and huge files.
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NONBLOCK)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as handle:
        if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(handle.fileno()).st_mode):
            fail(label + " must be a regular file: " + str(path))
        raw = handle.read(limit + 1)
    if len(raw) > limit:
        fail(label + " is too large: " + str(path))
    return raw.decode("utf-8")


def read_pyvenv_cfg(path):
    # Same key = value format that Python's own startup code reads.
    # Parsed only: nothing from the venv is executed on the host.
    config = {}
    for line in read_small_text(path, 65536, "pyvenv.cfg").splitlines():
        key, separator, value = line.partition("=")
        if separator:
            config[key.strip().lower()] = value.strip()
    return config


def venv_details(project, venv, label="Virtualenv"):
    # Parse, never execute: venv files may be agent-written.
    resolved = venv.resolve(strict=True)
    if not resolved.is_dir():
        fail(label + " is not a directory: " + str(venv))
    config = read_pyvenv_cfg(resolved / "pyvenv.cfg")
    bin_dir = venv / "bin"
    if not bin_dir.is_dir():
        fail(label + " has no bin directory: " + str(venv))
    for name in ("python", "python3"):
        if (bin_dir / name).exists():
            interpreter = (bin_dir / name).resolve(strict=True)
            break
    else:
        fail(label + " has no bin/python: " + str(venv))
    home = config.get("home", "")
    if not os.path.isabs(home):
        fail("pyvenv.cfg has no absolute home entry: " + str(resolved / "pyvenv.cfg"))
    home = Path(os.path.normpath(home))
    # The venv itself, the base install named by pyvenv.cfg, and the prefix
    # of the interpreter bin/python resolves to (framework builds differ).
    reads = []
    for candidate in (venv, resolved, home.parent, home.resolve().parent, interpreter.parent.parent):
        if candidate.is_relative_to(project) and candidate.resolve().is_relative_to(project):
            continue
        for spelled in (candidate, candidate.resolve()):
            reject_protected_grant(spelled)
            if account_home().is_relative_to(spelled):
                fail(label + " read grant would expose your home or an ancestor: " + str(spelled))
            reads.append(str(spelled))
    return {"path": str(venv), "resolved": str(resolved), "bin": str(bin_dir),
            "python": str(interpreter), "allowRead": list(dict.fromkeys(reads))}


def detect_virtualenv(project, mode):
    if mode == "off":
        return None
    value = os.environ.get("VIRTUAL_ENV")
    if value:
        if "\0" in value or not os.path.isabs(value):
            fail("VIRTUAL_ENV must be an absolute path: " + json.dumps(value, ensure_ascii=True))
        return venv_details(project, Path(os.path.normpath(value)))
    if mode != "auto":
        return None
    local = project / ".venv"
    if not os.path.lexists(local):
        return None
    # Agent-writable location: never follow a planted symlink out of the
    # project.
    if local.is_symlink() or not local.is_dir():
        fail(".venv must be a real directory inside the project, not a symlink: " + str(local))
    if not (local / "pyvenv.cfg").is_file():
        fail(".venv has no pyvenv.cfg; recreate it or use --no-auto-venv: " + str(local))
    return venv_details(project, local)


def detect_tools_venv(project, spec, filesystem):
    # A shared, host-maintained venv (e.g. openpyxl, pandas) that every
    # agent may use but none may change.
    venv = resolve_project_path(project, spec, canonical=False)
    venv = Path(os.path.normpath(venv))
    if not (venv / "pyvenv.cfg").is_file():
        fail("toolsVenv is not a virtualenv (no pyvenv.cfg): " + str(venv))
    details = venv_details(project, venv, "Tools venv")
    for spelled in (venv, Path(details["resolved"])):
        if spelled.is_relative_to(project) or project.is_relative_to(spelled):
            fail("toolsVenv must be outside the project so agents cannot modify it: " + str(spelled))
        for entry in filesystem.get("allowWrite", []):
            granted = Path(entry["path"] if isinstance(entry, dict) else entry)
            if spelled.is_relative_to(granted) or granted.is_relative_to(spelled):
                fail("toolsVenv must stay read-only, but global allowWrite covers it: " + str(granted))
    return details


TOOLS_PYTHON = "toolpy"
# Launcher defaults that setEnv may replace: toolchain homes. Reads and
# writes still follow the policy, so pointing one at a host folder needs a
# matching allowRead and never grants writes outside the project.
OVERRIDABLE_ENV = {"RUSTUP_HOME", "CARGO_HOME", "TMPDIR"}
# Overridable only into this project's {cache} folder: tests that create
# Git repositories or shell rc files in temp folders hit srt's built-in
# blocks inside the project, but not in the cache outside it.
CACHE_ONLY_ENV = {"TMPDIR"}


def install_tools_wrapper(home, tools):
    # A symlink to a venv's python elsewhere loses the venv (Python looks for
    # pyvenv.cfg beside the invoked path), so write a tiny exec wrapper. The
    # directory is on the agent PATH and therefore write-denied to agents,
    # but .local above it is not: walk without following symlinks.
    fd = open_private_dir(home, ".local/bin")
    try:
        if tools is None:
            try:
                os.unlink(TOOLS_PYTHON, dir_fd=fd)
            except FileNotFoundError:
                pass
            return
        script = "#!/bin/sh\nexec " + shlex.quote(str(Path(tools["bin"]) / "python")) + ' "$@"\n'
        temporary = ".toolpy-" + os.urandom(8).hex()
        out = os.open(temporary, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o500, dir_fd=fd)
        try:
            with os.fdopen(out, "w") as handle:
                handle.write(script)
                os.fchmod(handle.fileno(), 0o500)
            os.replace(temporary, TOOLS_PYTHON, src_dir_fd=fd, dst_dir_fd=fd)
        finally:
            try:
                os.unlink(temporary, dir_fd=fd)
            except FileNotFoundError:
                pass
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


# Paths in an agent home that the launcher itself manages.
TEMPLATE_RESERVED = (".local/bin", ".claude/sessions")
TEMPLATE_FILE_LIMIT = 1024 * 1024


def template_directory(project, settings):
    # home/ next to the global config (~/.config/srt-agent/home), as spelled.
    return resolve_project_path(project, str(settings), canonical=False).parent / "home"


def scan_template(project, settings):
    # home/common/... and home/<agent>/..., mirroring the agent home.
    # Regular files are copied ("managed": rewritten every launch and
    # write-protected); files under <scope>/.seed/ are copied only when
    # missing and left writable. A link to a file outside the template is
    # recreated as a link (live edits), its target granted read-only. Links
    # inside the template are followed and copied. Folders reached through
    # links, and special files, are refused.
    root = template_directory(project, settings)
    if not os.path.lexists(root):
        return {}
    if not root.is_dir():
        fail(str(root) + " must be a folder")
    real_root = root.resolve()
    forbidden = [storage_parent(), approval_directory().parent]
    scopes = {}
    for scope_entry in sorted(root.iterdir()):
        scope = scope_entry.name
        if scope.startswith("."):
            continue
        if not scope_entry.is_dir() or scope_entry.is_symlink():
            fail(str(scope_entry) + ": the template holds folders named common or after an agent")
        if scope != "common" and not AGENT_NAME.match(scope):
            fail("Invalid template folder " + str(scope_entry) + "; use common or an agent name")
        entries = {}

        def walk(directory, relative, seed):
            for entry in sorted(os.scandir(directory), key=lambda e: e.name):
                if entry.name == ".DS_Store":
                    continue
                if not relative and entry.name == ".seed" and not seed:
                    if not entry.is_dir(follow_symlinks=False):
                        fail(entry.path + " must be a folder")
                    walk(entry.path, (), True)
                    continue
                rel = relative + (entry.name,)
                text = "/".join(rel)
                if any(text == r or text.startswith(r + "/") for r in TEMPLATE_RESERVED):
                    fail(entry.path + ": " + text + " is managed by the launcher itself")
                if entry.is_symlink():
                    try:
                        target = Path(entry.path).resolve(strict=True)
                    except (FileNotFoundError, RuntimeError):
                        fail("Template link is broken: " + entry.path)
                    if not target.is_file():
                        fail("Template link must point to a file: " + entry.path + " -> " + str(target))
                    if not target.is_relative_to(real_root):
                        if seed:
                            fail("Seed files must be real files, not links: " + entry.path)
                        if any(target.is_relative_to(f) or target.is_relative_to(f.resolve()) for f in forbidden):
                            fail("Template link points into srt-agent's own storage: " + entry.path)
                        entries[text] = {"kind": "link", "target": str(target), "source": entry.path}
                        continue
                    source = target
                elif entry.is_dir(follow_symlinks=False):
                    walk(entry.path, rel, seed)
                    continue
                elif entry.is_file(follow_symlinks=False):
                    source = Path(entry.path)
                else:
                    fail("Template entries must be files, folders or links to files: " + entry.path)
                if source.stat().st_size > TEMPLATE_FILE_LIMIT:
                    fail("Template file is larger than 1 MiB: " + entry.path)
                data = read_regular(source)
                entries[text] = {"kind": "seed" if seed else "managed", "data": data,
                                 "sha256": hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest(), "source": entry.path}

        walk(scope_entry, (), False)
        scopes[scope] = entries
    return scopes


def template_summary(scopes):
    # For the approval: what is bound (hashes, link targets) and what is
    # shown (text content). Linked files are live, so only the link is bound.
    bound, shown = {}, {}
    for scope, entries in sorted(scopes.items()):
        for rel, entry in sorted(entries.items()):
            key = scope + "/" + rel
            if entry["kind"] == "link":
                bound[key] = "link -> " + entry["target"]
                shown[key] = bound[key]
                continue
            bound[key] = entry["kind"] + " " + entry["sha256"]
            try:
                text = entry["data"].decode("utf-8")
            except UnicodeDecodeError:
                text = "<binary, " + str(len(entry["data"])) + " bytes, sha256 " + entry["sha256"] + ">"
            shown[key] = ("(seed: copied once) " if entry["kind"] == "seed" else "") + text
    return bound, shown


def template_for(scopes, agent, home_mode):
    # common first, then the agent's own folder (which wins). In a shared
    # home, two agents' templates may not both claim a path.
    chosen = dict(scopes.get("common", {}))
    chosen.update(scopes.get(agent, {}))
    if home_mode == "shared":
        owners = {}
        for scope, entries in scopes.items():
            if scope == "common":
                continue
            for rel in entries:
                if rel in owners:
                    fail("With agentHome shared, the templates of " + owners[rel] + " and " + scope
                         + " both write " + rel + "; keep it in one of them, or in common")
                owners[rel] = scope
    return chosen


def apply_template(home, manifest_path, chosen):
    # Writes into the agent home, which the agent controls: every step goes
    # through directory descriptors opened without following links, and
    # files are replaced by rename, so a planted link cannot redirect a
    # write. A file the launcher did not write before is kept as a backup.
    try:
        manifest = json.loads(manifest_path.read_text()) if manifest_path.is_file() else {}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        manifest = {}
    notes, written = [], {}

    def current_sha(fd, name):
        try:
            info = os.lstat(name, dir_fd=fd)
        except FileNotFoundError:
            return None, None
        if stat.S_ISLNK(info.st_mode):
            return "link", "link -> " + os.readlink(name, dir_fd=fd)
        if stat.S_ISREG(info.st_mode):
            handle = os.open(name, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW, dir_fd=fd)
            with os.fdopen(handle, "rb") as stream:
                return "file", hashlib.sha256(stream.read()).hexdigest()
        return "other", None

    def make_room(fd, name, rel, kind):
        if kind is None:
            return
        if kind == "other":
            fail("Agent home has a folder or special file where the template puts " + rel)
        recorded = manifest.get(rel)
        _, now = current_sha(fd, name)
        if recorded is not None and recorded == now:
            return  # ours, unchanged: simply replaced
        backup = name + ".srt-agent-backup-" + time.strftime("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S")
        os.rename(name, backup, src_dir_fd=fd, dst_dir_fd=fd)
        notes.append("kept the previous " + rel + " as " + backup)

    for rel, entry in sorted(chosen.items()):
        parent, name = os.path.split(rel)
        if parent:
            private_dir(home, parent)
        fd = open_private_dir(home, parent) if parent else os.open(home, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY)
        try:
            kind, now = current_sha(fd, name)
            if entry["kind"] == "seed":
                if kind is None:
                    _write_file(fd, name, entry["data"])
                continue
            want = entry["sha256"] if entry["kind"] == "managed" else "link -> " + entry["target"]
            if now == want:
                written[rel] = want
                continue
            make_room(fd, name, rel, kind)
            if entry["kind"] == "managed":
                _write_file(fd, name, entry["data"])
            else:
                temporary = ".srt-agent-link-" + os.urandom(8).hex()
                os.symlink(entry["target"], temporary, dir_fd=fd)
                os.replace(temporary, name, src_dir_fd=fd, dst_dir_fd=fd)
            written[rel] = want
        finally:
            os.close(fd)
    # Files the template no longer lists: removed if still exactly as the
    # launcher wrote them, otherwise left alone with a note.
    for rel, recorded in manifest.items():
        if rel in written:
            continue
        if chosen.get(rel, {}).get("kind") == "seed":
            continue  # was managed, now a seed: the existing copy becomes the agent's
        parent, name = os.path.split(rel)
        try:
            fd = open_private_dir(home, parent) if parent else os.open(home, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY)
        except (OSError, SystemExit):
            continue
        try:
            _, now = current_sha(fd, name)
            if now == recorded:
                os.unlink(name, dir_fd=fd)
            elif now is not None:
                notes.append(rel + " is no longer in the template but was changed; left in place")
        finally:
            os.close(fd)
    temporary = manifest_path.with_name(manifest_path.name + ".tmp")
    temporary.write_text(json.dumps(written, indent=2, sort_keys=True))
    os.replace(temporary, manifest_path)
    for note in notes:
        print("srt-agent: template: " + note, file=sys.stderr)
    return written


def _write_file(fd, name, data):
    temporary = ".srt-agent-file-" + os.urandom(8).hex()
    out = os.open(temporary, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o600, dir_fd=fd)
    try:
        with os.fdopen(out, "wb") as handle:
            handle.write(data)
        os.replace(temporary, name, src_dir_fd=fd, dst_dir_fd=fd)
    finally:
        try:
            os.unlink(temporary, dir_fd=fd)
        except FileNotFoundError:
            pass


def venv_mode(requested, options):
    return requested or ("auto" if options.get("autoVenv") else "env")


def open_private_dir(root, relative):
    # Like private_dir, but only opens: returns a descriptor for root/relative
    # reached without following symlinks in any component below root. root
    # itself must be a folder agents cannot replace.
    fd = os.open(root, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY)
    try:
        for part in Path(relative).parts:
            try:
                child = os.open(part, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW, dir_fd=fd)
            except OSError as error:
                if error.errno in (errno.ELOOP, errno.ENOTDIR):
                    fail("Refusing a symlink or non-directory in private storage: " + str(Path(root) / relative))
                raise
            os.close(fd)
            fd = child
            if os.fstat(fd).st_uid != os.getuid():
                fail("Private directory is not owned by you: " + str(Path(root) / relative))
    except BaseException:
        os.close(fd)
        raise
    return fd


def private_dir(root, relative):
    # Walk with directory descriptors and O_NOFOLLOW so a concurrently
    # running agent cannot swap a component for a symlink between the check
    # and the mkdir/chmod (both happen relative to an already-opened fd).
    current = Path(root)
    fd = os.open(current, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY)
    try:
        for part in Path(relative).parts:
            if part in ("", ".", "..") or "/" in part:
                fail("Invalid private directory component: " + part)
            current = current / part
            try:
                os.mkdir(part, 0o700, dir_fd=fd)
            except FileExistsError:
                pass
            try:
                child = os.open(part, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW, dir_fd=fd)
            except OSError as error:
                if error.errno in (errno.ELOOP, errno.ENOTDIR):
                    fail("Refusing a symlink or non-directory in private storage: " + str(current))
                raise
            os.close(fd)
            fd = child
            if os.fstat(fd).st_uid != os.getuid():
                fail("Private directory is not owned by you: " + str(current))
            os.fchmod(fd, 0o700)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    return current


def literal(path):
    value = str(path)
    return {"path": value, "literal": True} if any(c in value for c in "*?[") else value


def unique_entries(entries):
    result = []
    seen = set()
    for entry in entries:
        key = json.dumps(entry, sort_keys=True)
        if key not in seen:
            seen.add(key)
            result.append(entry)
    return result


def messaging_scope(value):
    if value is True:
        return "project"
    if value is False:
        return "off"
    if isinstance(value, str) and value in ("off", "project", "global"):
        return value
    fail("Cross-session messaging scope must be off, project, or global (true/false mean project/off)")


def env_allowed(name):
    upper = name.upper()
    return not (upper in FORBIDDEN_ENV or upper.startswith(FORBIDDEN_ENV_PREFIXES) or PROXY_ENV.match(name))


def validate_env_patterns(values, label):
    if not isinstance(values, list) or any(not isinstance(v, str) or not ENV_PATTERN.match(v) for v in values):
        fail(label + " must be an array of variable names (a trailing * matches a prefix)")
    for value in values:
        if not value.endswith("*") and not env_allowed(value):
            fail(label + " cannot pass launcher-managed variable " + value)
    return list(values)


def validate_set_env(values, label):
    if not isinstance(values, dict):
        fail(label + " must be an object of NAME: string")
    for name, value in values.items():
        if not ENV_NAME.match(name) or not isinstance(value, str) or "\0" in value:
            fail(label + " must map variable names to strings")
        if name in CACHE_ONLY_ENV:
            if not uses_cache(value):
                fail(label + "." + name + ' may only be set to a {cache} folder, e.g. "{cache}/tmp"')
        elif not env_allowed(name):
            fail(label + " cannot set launcher-managed variable " + name)
    return dict(values)


GLOBAL_LAUNCHER_KEYS = ("crossSessionMessaging", "passEnv", "agents", "autoVenv", "toolsVenv", "path", "setEnv",
                        "groups", "agentHome", "baseSettings")
GROUP_LAUNCHER_KEYS = ("path", "setEnv")
PROJECT_LAUNCHER_KEYS = ("path", "setEnv", "agentHome")
# srt's on/off settings. Any layer may set them (imported srt file, global
# config, groups, project), later layers winning; anything that loosens
# security is named in its own approval prompt. allowPty must stay true:
# every agent runs on its own pseudo-terminal inside the sandbox.
SWITCHES = {
    "allowLocalBinding": ("network", "agents may run servers listening on this Mac"),
    "allowAllUnixSockets": ("network", "EVERY Unix socket, including Docker's (root) and agents holding your keys"),
    "enableWeakerNestedSandbox": (None, "a weaker sandbox, meant for running inside Docker"),
    "enableWeakerNetworkIsolation": (None, "weaker network isolation"),
    "allowAppleEvents": (None, "agents may script other apps outside the sandbox"),
}
SRT_LISTS = {
    "network": ("allowedDomains", "deniedDomains", "allowUnixSockets", "allowMachLookup"),
    "filesystem": ("allowRead", "denyRead", "allowWrite", "denyWrite"),
}


def take_switches(values, section, label):
    # Booleans only. allowPty may be written (srt files carry it) but only
    # as true. Proxy ports and other srt internals are not accepted at all.
    found = {}
    for key, (where, _) in SWITCHES.items():
        if where == section and key in values:
            if not isinstance(values[key], bool):
                fail(label + ": " + (key if section is None else section + "." + key) + " must be true or false")
            found[key] = values[key]
    if section is None and "allowPty" in values and values["allowPty"] is not True:
        fail(label + ": allowPty must be true; agents run on their own pseudo-terminal inside the sandbox")
    return found


def flat_layer(data, label, launcher_keys, other_keys=()):
    # Every config file is flat: srt's two lists (network, filesystem) next
    # to the launcher's own keys. Internally the launcher keys are grouped
    # under "srtAgent" so the rest of the code sees one shape. Only the
    # named srt lists are ever forwarded to srt; any other key, at any level,
    # is refused rather than passed through or ignored.
    if not isinstance(data, dict):
        fail(label + " must be a JSON object")
    if "srtAgent" in data:
        fail(label + ": the srtAgent wrapper is gone; move its keys (" + ", ".join(launcher_keys)
             + ") to the top level of the same object")
    top_switches = tuple(k for k, (section, _) in SWITCHES.items() if section is None) + ("allowPty",)
    allowed = ("network", "filesystem") + tuple(launcher_keys) + tuple(other_keys) + top_switches
    unknown = sorted(set(data) - set(allowed))
    if unknown:
        fail(label + " does not support " + ", ".join(unknown) + ". Supported: " + ", ".join(allowed))
    internal = {key: value for key, value in data.items() if key not in launcher_keys and key not in top_switches}
    switches = take_switches(data, None, label)
    for section, lists in SRT_LISTS.items():
        values = internal.get(section, {})
        if not isinstance(values, dict):
            fail(label + "." + section + " must be an object")
        section_switches = tuple(k for k, (where, _) in SWITCHES.items() if where == section)
        extra = sorted(set(values) - set(lists) - set(section_switches))
        if extra:
            fail(label + "." + section + " does not support " + ", ".join(extra) + ". Supported: "
                 + ", ".join(lists + section_switches))
        if section_switches and any(k in values for k in section_switches):
            switches.update(take_switches(values, section, label))
            internal[section] = {k: v for k, v in values.items() if k not in section_switches}
    if switches:
        internal["switches"] = switches
    launcher = {key: data[key] for key in launcher_keys if key in data}
    if launcher:
        internal["srtAgent"] = launcher
    return internal


def flat_global(data, label):
    internal = flat_layer(data, label, GLOBAL_LAUNCHER_KEYS)
    groups = internal.get("srtAgent", {}).get("groups")
    if isinstance(groups, dict):
        internal["srtAgent"]["groups"] = {
            name: flat_layer(group, label + ": groups." + str(name), GROUP_LAUNCHER_KEYS, ("remove", "extends"))
            for name, group in groups.items()}
    return internal


def validate_group(group, label):
    # Same shape as a project override, plus network.allowedDomains: groups
    # live in the global settings, which you alone write and approve.
    if not isinstance(group, dict) or set(group) - {"filesystem", "network", "remove", "srtAgent", "extends", "switches"}:
        fail(label + " supports filesystem, network, remove, extends, path and setEnv only")
    extends = group.get("extends", [])
    if not isinstance(extends, list) or any(not isinstance(e, str) or not GROUP_NAME.fullmatch(e) for e in extends):
        fail(label + '.extends must be an array of group names like "php-common"')
    filesystem = group.get("filesystem", {})
    if not isinstance(filesystem, dict) or set(filesystem) - set(REMOVABLE_LISTS["filesystem"]):
        fail(label + ".filesystem supports " + ", ".join(REMOVABLE_LISTS["filesystem"]) + " only")
    for name, entries in filesystem.items():
        if not isinstance(entries, list) or any(not isinstance(e, str) or not e for e in entries):
            fail(label + ".filesystem." + name + " must be an array of nonempty strings")
    network = group.get("network", {})
    if not isinstance(network, dict) or set(network) - set(REMOVABLE_LISTS["network"]):
        fail(label + ".network supports " + ", ".join(REMOVABLE_LISTS["network"]) + " only")
    validate_domains(network.get("allowedDomains", []), label + ".network.allowedDomains")
    validate_domains(network.get("deniedDomains", []), label + ".network.deniedDomains")
    for name in ("allowUnixSockets", "allowMachLookup"):
        values = network.get(name, [])
        if not isinstance(values, list) or any(not isinstance(v, str) or not v for v in values):
            fail(label + ".network." + name + " must be an array of nonempty strings")
    validate_removals(group.get("remove", {}))
    launcher = group.get("srtAgent", {})
    validate_path_entries(launcher.get("path", []), label + ".path")
    validate_set_env(launcher.get("setEnv", {}), label + ".setEnv")
    return group


def validate_groups(groups):
    if not isinstance(groups, dict):
        fail("Global groups must be an object")
    for name, group in groups.items():
        if not isinstance(name, str) or not GROUP_NAME.fullmatch(name):
            fail("Invalid group name in groups: " + json.dumps(name, ensure_ascii=True))
        validate_group(group, "groups." + name)
    return groups


SYSTEM_LIBRARY_ROOTS = ("/usr/lib/", "/System/")
HOMEBREW_PREFIXES = (Path("/opt/homebrew"), Path("/usr/local"))


class ToolInspection:
    # Finds what a program needs to read: its own files, its Homebrew
    # formula and that formula's runtime dependencies (from Homebrew's
    # INSTALL_RECEIPT.json, the records brew deps uses), libraries it links
    # (otool -L, following @rpath), and for scripts the interpreter named in
    # the shebang, recursively. Nothing found is executed.
    def __init__(self):
        self.grants, self.formulae, self.seen, self.notes = [], {}, set(), []

    def grant(self, path):
        text = str(path)
        if text not in self.grants:
            self.grants.append(text)

    def formula_of(self, path):
        for prefix in HOMEBREW_PREFIXES:
            cellar = prefix / "Cellar"
            if path.is_relative_to(cellar) and len(path.relative_to(cellar).parts) >= 2:
                formula, version = path.relative_to(cellar).parts[:2]
                return prefix, formula, version
        return None

    def package_of(self, path):
        # Programs that need the folder around them, granted as one unit:
        # - a global npm package (npm install -g): that package's folder
        #   under lib/node_modules, never lib/ itself;
        # - a Composer install (composer global require, or a project's
        #   vendor/bin): the vendor folder, which holds the autoloader. Not
        #   its parent, where Composer keeps auth.json;
        # - a Python virtualenv (uv tool, pipx): the whole environment,
        #   whose interpreter and packages the script needs.
        if (path.name.startswith("python") and path.parent.name == "bin"
                and any(path.parent.parent.glob("lib/python3*"))):
            return path.parent.parent  # a self-contained Python (uv, python.org): bin/ and its lib/
        for ancestor in path.parents:
            if (ancestor / "pyvenv.cfg").is_file():
                return ancestor
            if ancestor.name == "vendor" and (ancestor / "autoload.php").is_file():
                return ancestor
        for prefix in HOMEBREW_PREFIXES:
            modules = prefix / "lib" / "node_modules"
            if path.is_relative_to(modules):
                parts = path.relative_to(modules).parts
                depth = 2 if parts and parts[0].startswith("@") else 1
                if len(parts) > depth:
                    return modules.joinpath(*parts[:depth])
        return None

    def add_formula(self, prefix, formula, version=None):
        if formula in self.formulae:
            return
        if version is None:
            try:
                version = (prefix / "opt" / formula).resolve(strict=True).name
            except OSError:
                self.notes.append("Homebrew dependency " + formula + " is not installed; skipped")
                return
        self.formulae[formula] = version
        self.grant(prefix / "Cellar" / formula)
        receipt = prefix / "Cellar" / formula / version / "INSTALL_RECEIPT.json"
        try:
            data = json.loads(read_small_text(receipt, 1024 * 1024, str(receipt)))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            self.notes.append("No readable Homebrew record for " + formula + "; its dependencies come from otool only")
            return
        for dependency in data.get("runtime_dependencies") or []:
            name = dependency.get("full_name") if isinstance(dependency, dict) else None
            if isinstance(name, str) and name:
                self.add_formula(prefix, name.split("/")[-1])

    def otool(self, *args):
        try:
            return subprocess.run(["/usr/bin/otool", *args], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30,
                                  check=False).stdout
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
            return ""

    def libraries(self, path, executable):
        rpaths, lines = [], self.otool("-l", str(path)).splitlines()
        for index, line in enumerate(lines):
            if line.strip() == "cmd LC_RPATH":
                for follow in lines[index + 1:index + 4]:
                    follow = follow.strip()
                    if follow.startswith("path "):
                        rpaths.append(follow[5:].rsplit(" (offset", 1)[0])
        found = []
        for line in self.otool("-L", str(path)).splitlines()[1:]:
            line = line.strip()
            if not line or line.startswith("(") or line.endswith(":"):
                continue
            name = line.split(" (compatibility", 1)[0].strip()
            candidates = [name]
            if name.startswith("@rpath/"):
                candidates = [r + name[len("@rpath"):] for r in rpaths]
            candidates = [c.replace("@loader_path", str(path.parent)).replace("@executable_path", str(executable.parent))
                          for c in candidates]
            for candidate in candidates:
                if candidate.startswith(SYSTEM_LIBRARY_ROOTS):
                    break  # the system's own libraries are readable globally
                if os.path.exists(candidate):
                    found.append(Path(candidate).resolve())
                    break
            else:
                if not name.startswith(SYSTEM_LIBRARY_ROOTS):
                    self.notes.append("Could not locate " + name + " (linked by " + str(path) + ")")
        return found

    def inspect(self, path, executable=None):
        real = path.resolve()
        if real in self.seen:
            return
        self.seen.add(real)
        executable = executable or real
        if str(real).startswith(("/usr/bin/", "/bin/", "/usr/sbin/", "/sbin/", "/usr/lib/", "/System/")):
            return  # part of macOS, readable globally
        formula = self.formula_of(real)
        package = self.package_of(real)
        if formula:
            self.add_formula(*formula)
        elif package:
            self.grant(package)  # the whole package, with its own dependencies
        else:
            self.grant(real)
        try:
            with open(real, "rb") as handle:
                head = handle.read(256)
        except OSError:
            return
        if head.startswith(b"#!"):
            words = head[2:].split(b"\n", 1)[0].decode("utf-8", "replace").split()
            if words and os.path.basename(words[0]) == "env":
                words = [w for w in words[1:] if not w.startswith("-")]
                interpreter = shutil.which(words[0]) if words else None
            else:
                interpreter = words[0] if words else None
            if interpreter:
                self.inspect(Path(interpreter))
            return
        for library in self.libraries(real, executable):
            self.inspect(library, executable)


def find_tool(name):
    if "/" in name:
        path = Path(name).expanduser().absolute()
    else:
        found = shutil.which(name)
        if not found:
            fail("No program named " + name + " on PATH")
        path = Path(found)
    if not path.is_file() or not os.access(path, os.X_OK):
        fail(str(path) + " is not an executable file")
    return path


def create_tool_group(settings, name, tools, force=False):
    directory = group_directory(account_home(), settings)
    if name is None:
        if len(tools) != 1:
            fail("Name the group when generating it for several tools, e.g. group create dev --tool rg --tool fd")
        name = "tool/" + re.sub(r"[^a-z0-9-]", "-", os.path.basename(tools[0]).lower()).strip("-")
    if not GROUP_NAME.fullmatch(name):
        fail("Invalid group name " + name + '; use e.g. "tool/rg"')
    inspection, described, extra_path = ToolInspection(), [], []
    standard = {"/usr/bin", "/bin", "/usr/sbin", "/sbin", "/usr/local/bin"} | {str(p / "bin") for p in HOMEBREW_PREFIXES}
    for tool in tools:
        path = find_tool(tool)
        if str(path.parent) not in standard and str(path.parent) not in extra_path:
            extra_path.append(str(path.parent))
        inspection.inspect(path)
        formula = inspection.formula_of(path.resolve())
        described.append(tool + ": " + str(path.resolve()) + (" (Homebrew " + formula[1] + " " + formula[2] + ")" if formula else ""))
    if not inspection.grants:
        fail("Nothing to grant: " + ", ".join(tools) + " " + ("is" if len(tools) == 1 else "are")
             + " part of macOS and already readable through the global config")
    target = directory / (name + ".jsonc")
    if os.path.lexists(target) and not force:
        fail(str(target) + " exists; use srt-agent group update " + name + " to regenerate it")
    lines = ['// srt-agent group "' + name + '", generated ' + time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") + " by:",
             "//     srt-agent group create " + name + "".join(" --tool " + shlex.quote(t) for t in tools),
             "// Regenerate after installing or upgrading: srt-agent group update " + name]
    lines += ["// " + line for line in described]
    lines += ["// Found from Homebrew records, otool -L and script interpreters. Not detectable:",
              "// config files and plugins the tool opens only while running; the sandbox",
              "// log names them on first use. Add them to allowRead below."]
    lines += ["// Note: " + note for note in inspection.notes]
    lines += ["// srt-agent:tools " + " ".join(shlex.quote(t) for t in tools), "{",
              '  "filesystem": {', '    "allowRead": [']
    lines += ["      " + json.dumps(grant, ensure_ascii=True) + "," for grant in inspection.grants]
    lines += ["    ],", "  },"]
    if extra_path:
        lines += ["  // Not in a standard PATH folder: added so agents (and language-server",
                  "  // plugins) find it by name. Everything in these folders becomes readable.",
                  '  "path": [' + ", ".join(json.dumps(p, ensure_ascii=True) for p in extra_path) + "],"]
    lines += ["}"]
    body = "\n".join(lines) + "\n"
    flat_layer(parse_jsonc(body.encode("utf-8"), str(target)), str(target), GROUP_LAUNCHER_KEYS, ("remove", "extends"))
    target.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    fd, temporary = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=".group-", dir=target.parent)
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as handle:
            handle.write(body)
        if force:
            os.replace(temporary, target)
        else:
            os.link(temporary, target)  # fails if it appeared meanwhile
    finally:
        if os.path.exists(temporary):
            os.unlink(temporary)
    print("Wrote " + str(target) + " (" + str(len(inspection.grants)) + " path" + ("" if len(inspection.grants) == 1 else "s") + ")")
    for grant in inspection.grants:
        print("  " + grant)
    for note in inspection.notes:
        print("  note: " + note)
    print('Projects use it with "extends": ["' + name + '"]')


def update_tool_group(settings, name):
    if not GROUP_NAME.fullmatch(name):
        fail("Invalid group name " + name)
    target = group_directory(account_home(), settings) / (name + ".jsonc")
    try:
        text = read_regular(target.resolve(strict=True)).decode("utf-8")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        fail("No group file " + str(target))
    for line in text.splitlines():
        if line.startswith("// srt-agent:tools "):
            create_tool_group(settings, name, shlex.split(line[len("// srt-agent:tools "):]), force=True)
            return
    fail(str(target) + " was not generated by group create (no srt-agent:tools line); edit it by hand")


def group_protections(project, settings):
    # Agents may neither add, edit nor retarget a group: deny writes to the
    # folder (both spellings) and to every group file's real target.
    directory = group_directory(project, settings)
    paths = [directory]
    if os.path.lexists(directory):
        paths.append(directory.resolve())
        for entry in directory.iterdir():
            if entry.is_dir() and not entry.name.startswith("."):
                paths += [entry, entry.resolve()]
        for _, (_, source, _) in group_files(project, settings).items():
            paths.append(Path(source["resolved_path"]))
    return list(dict.fromkeys(paths))


def group_directory(project, settings):
    # groups/ next to the global config, as spelled (~/.config/srt-agent/
    # groups), even when config.jsonc itself is a symlink into dotfiles.
    return resolve_project_path(project, str(settings), canonical=False).parent / "groups"


def group_files(project, settings):
    # One group per groups/<name>.jsonc; the file name is the group name.
    # Hidden files and anything not ending in .jsonc (editor backups) are
    # skipped; a .jsonc whose name is not a valid group name is refused, so
    # a typo cannot silently drop a group. Symlinks (stow) are followed.
    # Returns {name: (internal group, source record, parsed file)}.
    directory = group_directory(project, settings)
    if not os.path.lexists(directory):
        return {}
    if not directory.is_dir():
        fail(str(directory) + " must be a folder of <group>.jsonc files")
    candidates = []
    for entry in sorted(directory.iterdir()):
        if entry.name.startswith("."):
            continue
        if entry.is_dir():
            # One namespace level: groups/<namespace>/<name>.jsonc
            if not re.fullmatch(GROUP_SEGMENT, entry.name):
                fail("Invalid group namespace folder " + str(entry) + "; use lowercase letters, digits and -")
            for inner in sorted(entry.iterdir()):
                if inner.name.startswith("."):
                    continue
                if inner.is_dir():
                    fail("Group namespaces are one level deep: " + str(inner))
                if inner.name.endswith(".jsonc"):
                    candidates.append((entry.name + "/" + inner.name[:-len(".jsonc")], inner))
        elif entry.name.endswith(".jsonc"):
            candidates.append((entry.name[:-len(".jsonc")], entry))
    found = {}
    for name, entry in candidates:
        if not GROUP_NAME.fullmatch(name):
            fail("Invalid group file name " + str(entry) + "; use lowercase letters, digits and -")
        try:
            resolved = entry.resolve(strict=True)
        except FileNotFoundError:
            fail("Group file is a broken link: " + str(entry))
        label = str(entry)
        data = parse_jsonc(read_regular(resolved), label)
        internal = flat_layer(data, label, GROUP_LAUNCHER_KEYS, ("remove", "extends"))
        validate_group(internal, label)
        found[name] = (internal, {"path": str(entry), "resolved_path": str(resolved),
                                  "content_sha256": settings_digest(data)}, data)
    return found


def expand_groups(references, groups, directory):
    # Depth first: a group's own "extends" come before it, in the order
    # listed. Each group is applied once, where it first appears, however
    # many paths lead to it. A group that reaches itself is refused.
    order, done = [], set()

    def visit(name, chain):
        if name in chain:
            fail("Group cycle: " + " -> ".join(chain[chain.index(name):] + [name]))
        if name not in groups:
            where = (" (from " + chain[-1] + ")") if chain else ""
            fail("Unknown group " + name + where + "; create " + str(directory / (name + ".jsonc"))
                 + " or define it under groups in the global settings")
        if name in done:
            return
        for parent in dict.fromkeys(groups[name].get("extends", [])):
            visit(parent, chain + [name])
        done.add(name)
        order.append(name)

    for reference in dict.fromkeys(references):
        visit(reference, [])
    return order


def global_groups(project, settings, with_sources=False):
    # Inline groups (in config.jsonc) and group files. Inline groups are
    # part of the global file, so approval binds them for every project;
    # group files are bound only by the projects that extend them.
    path = resolve_project_path(project, str(settings), canonical=False).resolve(strict=True)
    data = flat_global(parse_jsonc(read_regular(path), str(path)), str(path))
    groups = dict(validate_groups(data.get("srtAgent", {}).get("groups", {})))
    sources = {}
    for name, (group, source, parsed) in group_files(project, settings).items():
        if name in groups:
            fail("Group " + name + " is defined both in " + str(path) + " and in " + source["path"]
                 + "; keep one")
        groups[name] = group
        sources[name] = (source, parsed)
    # Check every group's extends now (unknown names, cycles), not only when
    # a project first reaches the broken one.
    expand_groups(sorted(groups), groups, group_directory(project, settings))
    return (groups, sources) if with_sources else groups


def merge_layers(layers):
    # Lists concatenate in order (duplicates dropped); setEnv: later wins.
    merged = {}
    for layer in layers:
        for section in ("filesystem", "network"):
            for name, entries in layer.get(section, {}).items():
                target = merged.setdefault(section, {}).setdefault(name, [])
                target.extend(e for e in entries if e not in target)
        for section, lists in layer.get("remove", {}).items():
            for name, entries in lists.items():
                target = merged.setdefault("remove", {}).setdefault(section, {}).setdefault(name, [])
                target.extend(e for e in entries if e not in target)
        if layer.get("switches"):
            merged.setdefault("switches", {}).update(layer["switches"])
        launcher = layer.get("srtAgent", {})
        if launcher:
            target = merged.setdefault("srtAgent", {})
            path = target.setdefault("path", [])
            path.extend(e for e in launcher.get("path", []) if e not in path)
            target.setdefault("setEnv", {}).update(launcher.get("setEnv", {}))
            if "agentHome" in launcher:
                target["agentHome"] = launcher["agentHome"]
    return merged


CACHE_PLACEHOLDER = "{cache}"


STORAGE_FORMAT = 1


def project_id(project):
    # Readable name for discoverability; the 96-bit digest of the resolved
    # project path is the identity. Renaming or moving a project gives it a
    # new identity (and fresh agent state) by design.
    name = re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9._-]", "_", project.name)[:40] or "project"
    return name + "-" + hashlib.sha256(os.fsencode(str(project))).hexdigest()[:24]


def storage_parent():
    return account_home() / ".local/share/srt-agent"


def storage_base():
    return storage_parent() / "projects"


def cache_base():
    return account_home() / "Library/Caches/srt-agent"


def project_storage_path(project):
    return storage_base() / project_id(project)


def project_cache_dir(project):
    # Per-project, outside the project tree: srt's built-in write blocks
    # (.vscode, .idea, .git hooks, shell rc files...) cover only the project,
    # so caches that unpack third-party trees (Cargo's crate sources) work
    # here. Nothing on the host opens this folder as a workspace, repository
    # or home, so those files are inert in it.
    return cache_base() / project_id(project)


def project_storage(project):
    # Persistent per-project agent state, outside the project so credentials
    # never sit in the repository tree, archives or synced project folders.
    # The root and its identity record are launcher-owned: agents get access
    # only to their own agents/<name> subtree, never to the root itself.
    parent = storage_parent()
    current = account_home()
    for part in parent.relative_to(current).parts:
        current /= part
        if current.is_symlink():
            fail("Agent storage must not contain symlinks: " + str(current))
    parent.mkdir(parents=True, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    if not parent.is_dir() or parent.stat().st_uid != os.getuid():
        fail("Agent storage must be a directory owned by you: " + str(parent))
    root = private_dir(parent, Path("projects") / project_id(project))
    record = root / "project.json"
    expected = {"format": STORAGE_FORMAT, "project": str(project)}
    for _ in range(2):
        try:
            fd = os.open(record, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK)
        except FileNotFoundError:
            # Write a complete record under a unique name, then publish it
            # with link(), which never replaces an existing file: concurrent
            # first launches either win or read the winner's full record.
            staged = root / (".project.json." + os.urandom(8).hex())
            fd = os.open(staged, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o600)
            try:
                with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as handle:
                    json.dump(expected, handle, indent=2)
                    handle.write("\n")
                    handle.flush()
                    os.fsync(handle.fileno())
                try:
                    os.link(staged, record, follow_symlinks=False)
                except FileExistsError:
                    continue  # a concurrent launch published first; verify theirs
            finally:
                staged.unlink(missing_ok=True)
            return root
        with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as handle:
            info = os.fstat(handle.fileno())
            if not stat.S_ISREG(info.st_mode) or info.st_uid != os.getuid():
                fail("Agent storage identity record must be a regular file owned by you: " + str(record))
            raw = handle.read(65537)
        try:
            data = json.loads(raw)
        except ValueError:
            data = None
        if data != expected:
            fail("Agent storage " + str(root) + " belongs to another project or is damaged (project.json does not "
                 "name " + str(project) + "). Inspect it, then move or delete it.")
        return root
    fail("Could not create the agent storage identity record: " + str(record))


def uses_cache(value):
    return value == CACHE_PLACEHOLDER or value.startswith(CACHE_PLACEHOLDER + "/")


def expand_env_value(value, project=None):
    # Only a leading ~/ (your account home) or {cache} (this project's cache
    # folder) expands; anything else is passed through as written.
    if value.startswith("~/"):
        return str(account_home() / value[2:])
    if uses_cache(value):
        rest = value[len(CACHE_PLACEHOLDER):].lstrip("/")
        if ".." in Path(rest).parts:
            fail("{cache} values must stay inside the cache folder: " + value)
        if project is None:
            fail("{cache} needs a project")
        return str(project_cache_dir(project) / rest) if rest else str(project_cache_dir(project))
    return value


AGENT_HOME_MODES = ("isolated", "shared")


def validate_agent_home(value, label):
    if value not in AGENT_HOME_MODES:
        fail(label + ' must be "isolated" or "shared"')
    return value


def validate_path_entries(entries, label):
    if not isinstance(entries, list) or any(
            not isinstance(e, str) or "\0" in e or "*" in e or ":" in e or not (e.startswith("~/") or os.path.isabs(e))
            for e in entries):
        fail(label + " must be an array of absolute or ~/ directories")
    return list(entries)


def validate_domains(values, label):
    if not isinstance(values, list) or any(
            not isinstance(v, str) or not re.fullmatch(r"(\*\.)?[a-z0-9]([a-z0-9-]*[a-z0-9])?(\.[a-z0-9]([a-z0-9-]*[a-z0-9])?)+", v)
            for v in values):
        fail(label + " must be an array of lower-case host names (optionally *.example.com)")
    return list(values)


def validate_agents(agents):
    if not isinstance(agents, dict):
        fail("Global agents must be an object")
    result = {}
    for name, spec in agents.items():
        if not isinstance(name, str) or not AGENT_NAME.match(name) or name in RESERVED_AGENT_NAMES or name in AGENT_ALIASES:
            fail("Invalid agent name in agents: " + json.dumps(name, ensure_ascii=True))
        label = "agents." + name
        builtin = name in AGENTS
        allowed_keys = {"binary", "network", "filesystem", "passEnv", "setEnv"} | (set() if builtin else {"homeEnv"})
        if not isinstance(spec, dict) or set(spec) - allowed_keys:
            fail(label + " supports only: " + ", ".join(sorted(allowed_keys)))
        # Same shape as the srt settings these entries add to.
        network = spec.get("network", {})
        if not isinstance(network, dict) or set(network) - {"allowedDomains"}:
            fail(label + ".network supports only: allowedDomains")
        filesystem = spec.get("filesystem", {})
        if not isinstance(filesystem, dict) or set(filesystem) - {"allowRead"}:
            fail(label + ".filesystem supports only: allowRead")
        entry = {}
        if "binary" in spec or not builtin:
            binary = spec.get("binary")
            if not isinstance(binary, str) or not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9._+-]+", binary):
                fail(label + ".binary must be a bare executable name")
            entry["binary"] = binary
        homes = spec.get("homeEnv", {})
        if not isinstance(homes, dict):
            fail(label + ".homeEnv must be an object")
        for variable, relative in homes.items():
            if not ENV_NAME.match(variable) or not env_allowed(variable):
                fail(label + ".homeEnv cannot use " + json.dumps(variable, ensure_ascii=True))
            if (not isinstance(relative, str) or not relative or os.path.isabs(relative)
                    or any(part in ("", ".", "..") for part in relative.split("/"))):
                fail(label + ".homeEnv paths must be relative paths inside the private HOME")
        entry["homeEnv"] = dict(homes)
        entry["allowedDomains"] = validate_domains(network.get("allowedDomains", []), label + ".network.allowedDomains")
        reads = filesystem.get("allowRead", [])
        if not isinstance(reads, list) or any(
                not isinstance(r, str) or "\0" in r or "*" in r or not (r.startswith("~/") or os.path.isabs(r))
                for r in reads):
            fail(label + ".filesystem.allowRead must be an array of absolute or ~/ paths (no globs)")
        entry["allowRead"] = list(reads)
        entry["passEnv"] = validate_env_patterns(spec.get("passEnv", []), label + ".passEnv")
        entry["setEnv"] = validate_set_env(spec.get("setEnv", {}), label + ".setEnv")
        result[name] = entry
    return result


AGENT_GROUP_KEYS = {"network": ("allowedDomains",), "filesystem": ("allowRead",)}


def agent_group(project, settings, agent):
    # groups/agent/<agent>.jsonc, loaded automatically for that agent (and
    # whatever it extends). It extends the agent's entry in the global
    # config, so it may hold what that entry holds that makes sense in a
    # group: network.allowedDomains, filesystem.allowRead, path, setEnv.
    # Returns (merged group or None, ordered names, {file name: source}).
    groups, sources = global_groups(project, settings, with_sources=True)
    name = "agent/" + agent
    if name not in groups:
        return None, [], {}
    order = expand_groups([name], groups, group_directory(project, settings))
    layers = []
    for reference in order:
        layer = copy.deepcopy(groups[reference])
        layer.pop("extends", None)
        extra = sorted(set(layer) - {"network", "filesystem", "srtAgent"})
        for section, keys in AGENT_GROUP_KEYS.items():
            extra += [section + "." + k for k in sorted(set(layer.get(section, {})) - set(keys))]
        if extra:
            extra = [{"switches": "allowLocalBinding/allowAllUnixSockets/other switches"}.get(x, x) for x in extra]
            fail(("Agent group " + name if reference == name else "Group " + reference + " (extended by " + name + ")")
                 + " has " + ", ".join(extra) + "; agent groups support only network.allowedDomains, "
                 "filesystem.allowRead, path, setEnv and extends")
        layers.append(layer)
    return merge_layers(layers), order, {n: sources[n] for n in order if n in sources}


def all_agent_groups(project, settings):
    # Every agent group and what it reaches, for the global approval: like
    # an agents.<name> entry in config.jsonc, a change asks every project.
    groups, sources = global_groups(project, settings, with_sources=True)
    bound = {}
    for name in sorted(g for g in groups if g.startswith("agent/")):
        order = expand_groups([name], groups, group_directory(project, settings))
        bound[name] = {"order": order,
                       "files": {n: sources[n][0]["content_sha256"] for n in order if n in sources}}
    shown = {sources[n][0]["path"]: sources[n][1]
             for entry in bound.values() for n in entry["order"] if n in sources}
    return bound, shown


def canonical_agent(name):
    name = AGENT_ALIASES.get(name, name)
    if not AGENT_NAME.match(name) or name in RESERVED_AGENT_NAMES:
        fail("Invalid agent name: " + json.dumps(name, ensure_ascii=True))
    return name


def agent_profile(name, custom):
    if name not in AGENTS and name not in custom:
        fail("Unknown agent " + json.dumps(name, ensure_ascii=True) + "; built-ins are "
             + ", ".join(sorted(AGENTS)) + " (define others under agents)")
    profile = copy.deepcopy(AGENTS.get(name, {
        "homeEnv": {}, "allowedDomains": [], "passEnv": [], "setEnv": {}, "prependArgs": [],
    }))
    profile.setdefault("allowRead", [])
    extra = custom.get(name, {})
    if "binary" in extra:
        profile["binary"] = extra["binary"]
    profile["homeEnv"].update(extra.get("homeEnv", {}))
    for key in ("allowedDomains", "allowRead", "passEnv"):
        profile[key] = list(dict.fromkeys(profile[key] + extra.get(key, [])))
    profile["setEnv"].update(extra.get("setEnv", {}))
    return profile


def all_home_env(custom):
    homes = {}
    for name in list(AGENTS) + sorted(custom):
        for variable, relative in agent_profile(name, custom)["homeEnv"].items():
            if homes.setdefault(variable, relative) != relative:
                fail("Agents disagree on the location for " + variable)
    return homes


def passthrough_env(patterns, managed):
    result = {}
    for name, value in os.environ.items():
        if name in managed or not env_allowed(name):
            continue
        for pattern in patterns:
            if (name.startswith(pattern[:-1]) if pattern.endswith("*") else name == pattern):
                result[name] = value
                break
    return result


def global_messaging_root(create=False):
    home = account_home()
    root = home / ".local/state/srt-agent-messaging"
    current = home
    for part in root.relative_to(home).parts:
        current /= part
        if current.is_symlink():
            fail("Global messaging storage must not contain symlinks: " + str(current))
    if create:
        root.mkdir(parents=True, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    if root.exists():
        if not root.is_dir() or root.stat().st_uid != os.getuid():
            fail("Global messaging storage must be a directory owned by you")
        if create:
            root.chmod(0o700)
    return root


def process_start(pid):
    try:
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return None
    except PermissionError:
        return "unknown"
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(["/bin/ps", "-p", str(pid), "-o", "lstart="],
                                stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, text=True, timeout=5,
                                env={"LC_ALL": "C", "TZ": "UTC", "PATH": "/usr/bin:/bin"})
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        # Restricted hosts may disallow process inspection. Retain a live
        # lease conservatively rather than risk changing its registry.
        return "unknown"
    return result.stdout.strip() if result.returncode == 0 and result.stdout.strip() else "unknown"


def registry_has_live_sessions(directory, project, global_registry):
    for entry in directory.glob("*.json"):
        if not entry.stem.isdecimal():
            continue
        pid = int(entry.stem)
        if not 0 < pid <= 2147483647:
            continue
        try:
            data = json.loads(read_regular(entry))
        except FileNotFoundError:
            continue
        if not isinstance(data, dict):
            fail("Invalid Claude session registry record: " + str(entry))
        if global_registry and isinstance(data.get("cwd"), str) and Path(data["cwd"]).is_absolute():
            if not Path(data["cwd"]).resolve().is_relative_to(project):
                continue
        if process_start(pid) is not None:
            return True
    return False


def activate_session_registry(project, home, scope):
    # Claude currently derives discovery records and peer auth keys from
    # CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/sessions. Share that directory, never credentials
    # or the rest of CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. Preserve project metadata when
    # selecting the global registry, and switch back reversibly.
    registry_scope = "global" if scope == "global" else "project"
    config = home / ".claude"
    active = config / "sessions"
    project_registry = config / "sessions.project"
    global_registry = global_messaging_root() / "sessions"
    state = private_dir(approval_directory(create=True).parent, "messaging-leases")
    fd = os.open(state / (project_key(project) + ".json"), os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK, 0o600)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "r+") as handle:
        info = os.fstat(handle.fileno())
        if not stat.S_ISREG(info.st_mode) or info.st_uid != os.getuid():
            fail("Messaging scope leases must be a regular file owned by you")
        fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        raw = handle.read(1024 * 1024 + 1)
        if len(raw) > 1024 * 1024:
            fail("Messaging lease file exceeds 1 MiB")
        records = json.loads(raw) if raw else []
        if not isinstance(records, list):
            fail("Invalid messaging scope leases")
        live = []
        for record in records:
            if not isinstance(record, dict) or type(record.get("pid")) is not int or record["pid"] <= 0 or record.get("scope") not in ("project", "global") or not isinstance(record.get("start"), str):
                fail("Invalid messaging scope lease")
            start = process_start(record["pid"])
            if start is None or (start != "unknown" and record["start"] != "unknown" and start != record["start"]):
                continue
            live.append(record)
        if any(record["scope"] != registry_scope for record in live):
            fail("Exit this project's running Claude sessions before switching between project and global messaging")
        # Work through a descriptor for CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR obtained with a
        # no-follow walk from the agent's home (whose own entry agents cannot
        # replace), and only *at operations below it: a concurrently running
        # agent swapping .claude or sessions for a symlink cannot redirect
        # these renames and links outside its own config.
        cfd = open_private_dir(home, ".claude")
        try:
            def entry(name):
                try:
                    return os.stat(name, dir_fd=cfd, follow_symlinks=False)
                except FileNotFoundError:
                    return None

            def ensure_project_registry():
                try:
                    os.mkdir("sessions.project", 0o700, dir_fd=cfd)
                except FileExistsError:
                    info = entry("sessions.project")
                    if info is None or not stat.S_ISDIR(info.st_mode) or info.st_uid != os.getuid():
                        fail("Claude sessions.project must be a directory owned by you")
                return str(project_registry)

            current_scope = "project"
            info = entry("sessions")
            if info is not None and stat.S_ISLNK(info.st_mode):
                target = os.readlink("sessions", dir_fd=cfd)
                if target == str(global_registry):
                    current_scope = "global"
                elif target != str(project_registry):
                    fail("Unexpected Claude sessions symlink target: " + str(active))
            elif info is not None and (not stat.S_ISDIR(info.st_mode) or info.st_uid != os.getuid()):
                fail("Claude sessions must be a directory owned by you")
            if current_scope != registry_scope:
                if registry_has_live_sessions(active, project, current_scope == "global"):
                    fail("Exit this project's running Claude sessions before switching messaging registry scope")
                if info is not None and not stat.S_ISLNK(info.st_mode):
                    if entry("sessions.project") is not None:
                        fail("Cannot preserve project registry: sessions.project already exists")
                    os.rename("sessions", "sessions.project", src_dir_fd=cfd, dst_dir_fd=cfd)
                target = str(global_registry) if registry_scope == "global" else ensure_project_registry()
                link = ".sessions-link-" + os.urandom(8).hex()
                try:
                    os.symlink(target, link, dir_fd=cfd)
                    os.replace(link, "sessions", src_dir_fd=cfd, dst_dir_fd=cfd)
                finally:
                    try:
                        os.unlink(link, dir_fd=cfd)
                    except FileNotFoundError:
                        pass
            elif info is None:
                if entry("sessions.project") is not None:
                    # Recover a previously preserved registry if an interrupted
                    # switch stopped between the rename and link publication.
                    os.symlink(ensure_project_registry(), "sessions", dir_fd=cfd)
                else:
                    os.mkdir("sessions", 0o700, dir_fd=cfd)
        finally:
            os.close(cfd)
        pid = os.getpid()
        start = process_start(pid)
        if start is None:
            fail("Cannot identify launcher process for the messaging scope lease")
        live = [record for record in live if record["pid"] != pid]
        live.append({"pid": pid, "start": start, "scope": registry_scope})
        handle.seek(0)
        json.dump(live, handle, ensure_ascii=True)
        handle.truncate()
        handle.flush()
        os.fchmod(handle.fileno(), 0o600)


def validate_removals(removals):
    if not isinstance(removals, dict) or set(removals) - set(REMOVABLE_LISTS):
        fail("Project remove supports filesystem and network objects only")
    result = {}
    for section, lists in REMOVABLE_LISTS.items():
        values = removals.get(section, {})
        if not isinstance(values, dict) or set(values) - set(lists):
            fail("Project remove." + section + " supports only: " + ", ".join(lists))
        for name, entries in values.items():
            if not isinstance(entries, list):
                fail("Project remove." + section + "." + name + " must be an array")
            for entry in entries:
                if section == "filesystem" and isinstance(entry, dict):
                    if set(entry) == {"path", "literal"} and entry["literal"] is True and isinstance(entry["path"], str) and entry["path"]:
                        continue
                if not isinstance(entry, str) or not entry:
                    fail("Removal entries must be nonempty strings or filesystem literal path objects")
            if entries:
                result.setdefault(section, {})[name] = unique_entries(entries)
    return result


def remove_global_entries(configuration, removals):
    # Match the original spelling and type: a glob here selects the global
    # rule itself, never files matching it. Work on a copy, not source data.
    result = copy.deepcopy(configuration)
    for section, lists in validate_removals(removals).items():
        inherited = result.get(section, {})
        if not isinstance(inherited, dict):
            fail("Global " + section + " must be an object")
        for name, targets in lists.items():
            entries = inherited.get(name, [])
            if not isinstance(entries, list):
                fail("Global " + section + "." + name + " must be an array")
            for target in targets:
                if target not in entries:
                    fail("No exact global entry for remove." + section + "." + name + ": " + json.dumps(target, ensure_ascii=True))
            inherited[name] = [entry for entry in entries if entry not in targets]
    return result


def global_filesystem(project, filesystem, allow_home=False):
    if not isinstance(filesystem, dict):
        fail("Global filesystem must be an object")
    result = copy.deepcopy(filesystem)
    if result.get("disabled"):
        fail("Global filesystem restrictions must not be disabled")

    def validate_grant(path):
        reject_protected_grant(path)
        if account_home().is_relative_to(path) and not (path == account_home() and allow_home):
            fail("Root/ancestor global grants are forbidden; whole-home access requires --allow-home: " + str(path))

    for name in ("allowRead", "allowWrite", "denyRead", "denyWrite"):
        entries = filesystem.get(name, [])
        if not isinstance(entries, list):
            fail("Global filesystem." + name + " must be an array")
        normalized = []
        for entry in entries:
            explicit_literal = isinstance(entry, dict)
            if explicit_literal:
                if set(entry) != {"path", "literal"} or entry["literal"] is not True:
                    fail("Global path objects must have path and literal: true")
                entry = entry["path"]
            if not isinstance(entry, str) or not entry:
                fail("Global filesystem paths must be nonempty strings")
            spelled = resolve_project_path(project, entry, canonical=False)
            is_glob = not explicit_literal and glob.has_magic(str(spelled))
            if name.startswith("allow"):
                if not Path(entry).is_absolute() and not entry.startswith("~") and spelled.resolve() == project:
                    fail("Global current-directory grants must be moved to the project override: " + entry)
                if is_glob:
                    # Resolve only concrete allow paths. Native glob allows
                    # can otherwise reopen a mandatory literal read denial.
                    # Refuse unbounded root/home patterns before traversing.
                    prefix = Path(spelled.anchor)
                    for component in spelled.parts[1:]:
                        if glob.has_magic(component):
                            break
                        prefix /= component
                    # A leaf prefix such as ~/.claude.json* is scoped to
                    # that namespace; ~/* would grant the whole home.
                    fixed_leaf = component.split("*", 1)[0].split("?", 1)[0].split("[", 1)[0]
                    if prefix.resolve() != account_home() or not fixed_leaf:
                        validate_grant(prefix.resolve())
                    candidates = [Path(p) for p in sorted(glob.glob(str(spelled), recursive=True))]
                    if spelled.exists() and spelled not in candidates:
                        candidates.append(spelled)
                else:
                    candidates = [spelled]
                for candidate in candidates:
                    resolved = candidate.resolve()
                    validate_grant(resolved)
                    if ".." not in candidate.parts:
                        validate_grant(candidate)
                        normalized.append(literal(candidate))
                    normalized.append(literal(resolved))
            elif is_glob:
                # Keep deny globs live so newly created files stay protected.
                normalized.append(str(spelled))
            else:
                normalized.extend((literal(spelled), literal(spelled.resolve())))
        result[name] = unique_entries(normalized)
    return result


BASE_SETTINGS_KEYS = SRT_LISTS  # what an imported srt file may contribute


def load_imported_base(project, spec, config_path):
    # baseSettings: an explicit, visible import of srt's own file as
    # inherited defaults for every agent: srt's lists and switches (switches
    # here are the first layer; later layers win). Anything else (unknown
    # keys, an srtAgent section, proxy ports) is refused rather than ignored.
    if not isinstance(spec, str) or "\0" in spec or not (spec.startswith("~/") or os.path.isabs(spec)):
        fail("Global baseSettings must be an absolute or ~/ path")
    name = resolve_project_path(project, spec, canonical=False)
    try:
        path = name.resolve(strict=True)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        fail("baseSettings names a missing file: " + str(name))
    if path == config_path:
        fail("baseSettings cannot name the srt-agent config itself")
    label = str(name) + " (baseSettings)"
    data = parse_jsonc(read_regular(path), label, comments=False)
    if not isinstance(data, dict):
        fail(label + " must be a JSON object")
    if "srtAgent" in data:
        fail(label + " contains an srtAgent section. Launcher options belong in the srt-agent config; move them there.")
    switches = take_switches(data, None, label)
    top = tuple(k for k, (where, _) in SWITCHES.items() if where is None) + ("allowPty",)
    unknown = sorted(set(data) - set(top) - set(BASE_SETTINGS_KEYS))
    if unknown:
        fail(label + " has settings srt-agent does not import: " + ", ".join(unknown)
             + ". Only network and filesystem lists are imported; remove them or stop importing this file.")
    for section, allowed in BASE_SETTINGS_KEYS.items():
        values = data.get(section, {})
        if not isinstance(values, dict):
            fail(label + "." + section + " must be an object")
        section_switches = tuple(k for k, (where, _) in SWITCHES.items() if where == section)
        switches.update(take_switches(values, section, label))
        lists = {k: v for k, v in values.items() if k not in section_switches}
        extra = sorted(set(lists) - set(allowed))
        if extra:
            fail(label + "." + section + " has settings srt-agent controls itself or does not import: " + ", ".join(extra)
                 + ". Imported: " + ", ".join(allowed) + ".")
        for key, entries in lists.items():
            # srt's own file holds plain strings only; launcher-style path
            # objects are not srt syntax and are refused here, not later.
            if not isinstance(entries, list) or any(not isinstance(e, str) or not e or "\0" in e for e in entries):
                fail(label + "." + section + "." + key + " must be an array of nonempty strings")
    return name, path, data, switches


def glob_regex(pattern):
    # srt path globs: * and ? stay within one folder name, ** crosses
    # folders, [...] is a character class.
    out, i = [], 0
    while i < len(pattern):
        if pattern.startswith("**", i):
            out.append(".*")
            i += 2
        elif pattern[i] == "*":
            out.append("[^/]*")
            i += 1
        elif pattern[i] == "?":
            out.append("[^/]")
            i += 1
        elif pattern[i] == "[" and "]" in pattern[i + 2:]:
            end = pattern.index("]", i + 2)
            body = pattern[i + 1:end]
            out.append("[" + ("^" + body[1:] if body.startswith("!") else body).replace("\\", "\\\\") + "]")
            i = end + 1
        else:
            out.append(re.escape(pattern[i]))
            i += 1
    return re.compile("".join(out))


def static_prefix(pattern):
    # The deepest folder every match of a glob lies inside.
    parts = Path(pattern).parts
    for index, part in enumerate(parts):
        if glob.has_magic(part):
            return Path(*parts[:index]) if index else Path("/")
    return Path(pattern)


def path_spellings(text):
    # As written and with symlinks resolved; for a glob only the literal
    # prefix is resolved and the rest reattached.
    if not glob.has_magic(text):
        return {text, os.path.realpath(text)}
    prefix = static_prefix(text)
    rest = os.path.relpath(text, prefix)
    return {text, os.path.join(os.path.realpath(prefix), rest)}


def refuse_ineffective_read_blocks(allow_entries, deny_entries):
    # In srt allowRead beats denyRead, so a block that a grant covers does
    # nothing. Refuse it rather than let it look protective. A grant INSIDE a
    # blocked area is the normal srt pattern and stays allowed.
    # What is checked (both as written and with symlinks resolved):
    #   literal grant vs literal block, literal grant vs glob block (via the
    #   block's literal prefix), glob grant vs literal block (the block or a
    #   parent matches), glob grant vs glob block (the block's literal prefix
    #   or a parent matches). Two globs that overlap only partly cannot be
    #   decided statically and are not refused, so this rejects many
    #   ineffective blocks but does not prove every remaining one works.
    # / and the account home are the launcher's own broad blocks; skipped.
    def text_of(entry):
        return entry["path"] if isinstance(entry, dict) else entry
    broad = {"/", str(account_home()), str(account_home().resolve())}
    grants = set()
    for entry in allow_entries:
        grants |= path_spellings(text_of(entry))
    for entry in deny_entries:
        written = text_of(entry)
        if written in broad:
            continue
        for blocked in path_spellings(written):
            anchor = static_prefix(blocked) if glob.has_magic(blocked) else Path(blocked)
            covered = [anchor, *anchor.parents]
            for granted in grants:
                if glob.has_magic(granted):
                    regex = glob_regex(granted)
                    hit = any(regex.fullmatch(str(p)) for p in covered)
                else:
                    hit = anchor == Path(granted) or anchor.is_relative_to(granted)
                if hit:
                    fail("denyRead " + written + " has no effect: allowRead " + granted + " covers it, and in srt "
                         "allowRead wins. Remove the denyRead, or replace the broad allowRead with narrower grants "
                         "that leave " + written + " out.")


def load_base_policy(project, settings, allow_home=False, removals=None):
    name = resolve_project_path(project, str(settings), canonical=False)
    path = name.resolve(strict=True)
    raw = read_regular(path)
    data = parse_jsonc(raw, str(path))
    internal = flat_global(data, str(path))
    merged, base_info, base_data = internal, None, None
    switches = {}
    declared = internal.get("srtAgent", {})
    if "baseSettings" in declared:
        base_name, base_path, base_data, base_switches = load_imported_base(project, declared["baseSettings"], path)
        # Imported entries come first and count as global entries, so an
        # approved project "remove" can drop them like any other default.
        merged = copy.deepcopy(internal)
        for section in BASE_SETTINGS_KEYS:
            for key, entries in base_data.get(section, {}).items():
                if key not in BASE_SETTINGS_KEYS[section]:
                    continue  # a switch, taken separately
                target = merged.setdefault(section, {}).setdefault(key, [])
                if not isinstance(target, list):
                    fail(str(path) + ": " + section + "." + key + " must be an array")
                merged[section][key] = unique_entries(entries + target)
        switches.update(base_switches)  # first layer
        base_info = {"path": str(base_name), "resolved_path": str(base_path), "content_sha256": settings_digest(base_data)}
    switches.update(merged.get("switches", {}))  # the global config wins over the import
    if not isinstance(merged.get("network"), dict):
        fail("Settings must contain a network object; refusing a policy fallback")
    removals = validate_removals({} if removals is None else removals)
    effective = remove_global_entries(merged, removals)
    effective.pop("switches", None)
    launcher_options = effective.pop("srtAgent", {})
    messaging_default = messaging_scope(launcher_options.get("crossSessionMessaging", "off"))
    options = {
        "crossSessionMessaging": messaging_default,
        "passEnv": validate_env_patterns(launcher_options.get("passEnv", []), "Global passEnv"),
        "agents": validate_agents(launcher_options.get("agents", {})),
    }
    # Optional keys appear only when configured, so existing approvals that
    # use neither stay valid.
    if "path" in launcher_options:
        options["path"] = validate_path_entries(launcher_options["path"], "Global path")
    if "groups" in launcher_options:
        validate_groups(launcher_options["groups"])
    if "agentHome" in launcher_options:
        options["agentHome"] = validate_agent_home(launcher_options["agentHome"], "Global agentHome")
    if "setEnv" in launcher_options:
        options["setEnv"] = validate_set_env(launcher_options["setEnv"], "Global setEnv")
    if "autoVenv" in launcher_options:
        if not isinstance(launcher_options["autoVenv"], bool):
            fail("Global autoVenv must be true or false")
        options["autoVenv"] = launcher_options["autoVenv"]
    filesystem = global_filesystem(project, effective.get("filesystem", {}), allow_home=allow_home)
    policy = {
        "path": str(name), "resolved_path": str(path),
        "content_sha256": settings_digest(data),
        # What the approval prompt diffs: the config, plus the imported file
        # when there is one, so a change to either is shown, not just flagged.
        "configuration": data if base_data is None else {**data, "(imported baseSettings)": base_data},
        "effective_configuration": effective,
        "launcher_options": options,
        "removals": removals,
        "filesystem": filesystem,
        "switches": switches,
    }
    template_bound, template_shown = template_summary(scan_template(project, settings))
    if template_bound:
        policy["template"] = template_bound
        policy["configuration"] = {**policy["configuration"], "(template home)": template_shown}
    agent_groups, agent_group_files = all_agent_groups(project, settings)
    if agent_groups:
        policy["agent_groups"] = agent_groups
        policy["configuration"] = {**policy["configuration"], "(agent group files)": agent_group_files}
    if base_info is not None:
        policy["base_settings"] = base_info
    if "toolsVenv" in launcher_options:
        spec = launcher_options["toolsVenv"]
        if not isinstance(spec, str) or "\0" in spec or not (spec.startswith("~/") or os.path.isabs(spec)):
            fail("Global toolsVenv must be an absolute or ~/ path")
        # Resolved grants are part of the approval identity: an upgrade that
        # moves the base interpreter asks again.
        policy["tools"] = detect_tools_venv(project, spec, filesystem)
    return policy


def write_policy(directory, agent, data):
    # Exclusive creation avoids reusing/taking input from any cached policy,
    # rejects pre-planted names, and keeps concurrent launches independent.
    fd, name = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=agent + "-", suffix=".json", dir=directory)
    path = Path(name)
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as handle:
            json.dump(data, handle, indent=2)
            handle.write("\n")
            handle.flush()
            os.fchmod(handle.fileno(), 0o400)
    except BaseException:
        path.unlink(missing_ok=True)
        raise
    # File mode is only an extra precaution. The directory lives outside the
    # project under the write-denied state directory.
    return path


def short_tmp(root, agent, target):
    link = Path("/tmp") / ("sa-" + str(os.getuid()) + "-" + project_key(root)[:16] + "-" + agent)
    try:
        os.symlink(str(target), str(link))
    except FileExistsError:
        if not link.is_symlink() or link.lstat().st_uid != os.getuid():
            fail("Temporary alias already exists with another owner or type: " + str(link))
        if link.resolve() != target:
            # Our own alias left over from an older layout: replace it
            # atomically. Agents cannot write /tmp, so only you could race it.
            staged = link.with_name(link.name + ".new-" + os.urandom(4).hex())
            os.symlink(str(target), str(staged))
            os.replace(staged, link)
    return link


def prepare(agent, project, settings, allow_local_binding=False, require_project_approval=True, allow_home=False,
            allow_cross_session_messaging=None, custom_messaging_socket=False, activate_messaging=True,
            requested_venv_mode=None):
    agent = canonical_agent(agent)
    requested_scope = None if allow_cross_session_messaging is None else messaging_scope(allow_cross_session_messaging)
    # Validate explicit opt-in before creating storage or temporary aliases.
    override_path, grants, project_data, project_raw = project_permissions(project, settings, allow_home=allow_home)
    base_policy = load_base_policy(project, settings, allow_home=allow_home, removals=grants["remove"])
    options = base_policy["launcher_options"]
    profile = agent_profile(agent, options["agents"])
    # groups/agent/<agent>.jsonc: extends this agent's entry. The agent's
    # entry in config.jsonc wins on setEnv, being the more specific.
    agent_extra, agent_groups_used, _ = agent_group(project, settings, agent)
    profile["groups"] = agent_groups_used
    profile.setdefault("path", [])
    if agent_extra:
        launcher = agent_extra.get("srtAgent", {})
        profile["allowRead"] = list(dict.fromkeys(agent_extra.get("filesystem", {}).get("allowRead", []) + profile["allowRead"]))
        profile["allowedDomains"] = list(dict.fromkeys(
            agent_extra.get("network", {}).get("allowedDomains", []) + profile["allowedDomains"]))
        profile["setEnv"] = {**launcher.get("setEnv", {}), **profile["setEnv"]}
        profile["path"] = list(launcher.get("path", []))
    if requested_scope not in (None, "off") and not profile.get("messaging"):
        fail("--allow-cross-session-messaging is supported for Claude only")
    settings_name = Path(base_policy["path"])
    settings = Path(base_policy["resolved_path"])
    base = base_policy["effective_configuration"]
    scope = (
        options["crossSessionMessaging"] if requested_scope is None else requested_scope
    ) if profile.get("messaging") else "off"
    if scope != "off" and custom_messaging_socket:
        fail("Launcher cross-session messaging cannot be combined with an agent --messaging-socket-path; use --no-cross-session-messaging to manage the path yourself")
    mode = venv_mode(requested_venv_mode, options)
    venv = detect_virtualenv(project, mode)
    if require_project_approval:
        require_approval(project, override_path, project_raw, project_data, grants, base_policy,
                         allow_home=allow_home, venv=venv, mode=mode)
    executable = find_binary(profile["binary"], agent, project)
    srt = find_binary("srt", "srt", project)
    storage = project_storage(project)
    agent_root = private_dir(storage, Path("agents") / agent)
    # isolated (default): agents/<agent>/home. shared: one shared/home for
    # this project's agents, a deliberate trust choice. Temp folders stay
    # per agent either way, and the modes use separate folders, so
    # switching never merges state.
    home_mode = grants.get("agentHome") or options.get("agentHome") or "isolated"
    home_root = private_dir(storage, "shared") if home_mode == "shared" else agent_root
    fresh_home = not (home_root / "home").is_dir()
    home = private_dir(home_root, "home")
    if fresh_home:
        other = ([storage / "shared/home"] if home_mode == "isolated" else
                 [entry / "home" for entry in (storage / "agents").iterdir() if (entry / "home").is_dir()])
        if any(path.is_dir() for path in other):
            print("srt-agent: note: using a new " + home_mode + " agent home (" + str(home) + "); the "
                  + ("shared" if home_mode == "isolated" else "isolated") + " home(s) are kept unchanged, "
                  "so agents may need to sign in again.", file=sys.stderr)
    # Every agent's config variable (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, CODEX_HOME, ...)
    # resolves inside THIS agent's home, so a codex run inside a Claude
    # session still never sees the codex agent's own credentials.
    homes = all_home_env(options["agents"])
    for directory in [".config", ".cache", ".local/share", ".local/state", ".local/bin"] + list(homes.values()):
        private_dir(home, directory)
    install_tools_wrapper(home, base_policy.get("tools"))
    template = template_for(scan_template(project, settings_name), agent, home_mode)
    applied = apply_template(home, home_root / "template.json", template)
    template_protected = [h / rel for h in dict.fromkeys((home, home.resolve()))
                          for rel, entry in template.items() if entry["kind"] != "seed"]
    template_reads = [entry["target"] for entry in template.values() if entry["kind"] == "link"]
    profile["template"] = sorted(applied)
    temp = private_dir(agent_root, "tmp")
    private_dir(temp, "run")
    policy_dir = private_dir(approval_directory(create=True).parent, "policies/" + project_key(project))
    # Agents get home and tmp, not agents/<name> itself: they cannot replace
    # either entry with a symlink, so the launcher's own walks from them stay
    # anchored.
    agent_paths = list(dict.fromkeys(p for d in (home, temp) for p in (d, d.resolve())))
    sibling_agents = sorted((set(AGENTS) | set(options["agents"]) | {
        entry.name for entry in (storage / "agents").iterdir() if entry.is_dir() and not entry.is_symlink()
    }) - {agent})
    if agent in sibling_agents or any(agent_root.is_relative_to(storage / "agents" / name) for name in sibling_agents):
        fail("Internal error: the running agent's own folder is in its write-deny list")
    sibling_paths = [storage / "agents" / name for name in sibling_agents]
    # srt runs OUTSIDE the sandbox: give it a temp folder agents can neither
    # read nor write (under the storage root, outside their grants), with
    # its own short alias for host-side Unix sockets. Never the agent's tmp.
    host_temp = private_dir(storage, Path("srt-tmp") / agent)
    host_temp_link = short_tmp(project, agent + "-srt", host_temp)
    temp_link = short_tmp(project, agent, temp)
    # macOS spells /tmp as /private/tmp. Keep the final symlink component:
    # resolve() on the whole link would return its project-local target and
    # lose the short alias spelling that Seatbelt also needs to permit.
    canonical_temp_link = temp_link.parent.resolve() / temp_link.name
    temp_paths = list(dict.fromkeys(str(p) for p in (temp, temp_link, canonical_temp_link)))
    messaging_paths = []
    messaging_filesystem_paths = []
    messaging = {"enabled": scope != "off", "scope": scope, "directory": None, "registry": None}
    if scope == "project":
        messaging_directory = private_dir(temp, "run/cc-socks")
        messaging_paths = list(dict.fromkeys(str(p) for p in (
            messaging_directory,
            temp_link / "run/cc-socks",
            canonical_temp_link / "run/cc-socks",
        )))
        messaging["directory"] = str(temp_link / "run/cc-socks")
        messaging["registry"] = str(home / ".claude/sessions")
    elif scope == "global":
        global_root = global_messaging_root(create=True)
        registry = private_dir(global_root, "sessions")
        sockets = private_dir(global_root, "sockets")
        global_link = short_tmp(account_home(), "claude-msg", global_root)
        canonical_link = global_link.parent.resolve() / global_link.name
        messaging_paths = list(dict.fromkeys(str(p) for p in (sockets, global_link / "sockets", canonical_link / "sockets")))
        messaging_filesystem_paths = [str(registry)] + messaging_paths
        messaging["directory"] = str(global_link / "sockets")
        messaging["registry"] = str(registry)
    if profile.get("messaging") and activate_messaging:
        activate_session_registry(project, home, scope)
    policy = copy.deepcopy(base)
    network = policy["network"]
    # Switches: off unless a layer (import, global, groups, project) turned
    # them on, all approved; --allow-local-binding turns local binding on for
    # this launch only. allowPty is always true.
    switches = effective_switches(base_policy, grants)
    if allow_local_binding:
        switches["allowLocalBinding"] = True
    policy["allowPty"] = True
    for key, (section, _) in SWITCHES.items():
        (policy if section is None else network)[key] = bool(switches.get(key, False))
    if grants.get("deniedDomains"):
        denied = network.setdefault("deniedDomains", [])
        network["deniedDomains"] = list(dict.fromkeys(denied + grants["deniedDomains"]))
    extra_domains = grants.get("allowedDomains", []) + profile["allowedDomains"]
    if extra_domains:
        domains = network.setdefault("allowedDomains", [])
        if not isinstance(domains, list):
            fail("network.allowedDomains must be an array")
        network["allowedDomains"] = list(dict.fromkeys(domains + extra_domains))
    # Expand network socket exceptions against the real home before changing HOME.
    if "allowUnixSockets" in network:
        values = network["allowUnixSockets"]
        if not isinstance(values, list) or any(not isinstance(p, str) or not p for p in values):
            fail("Base network.allowUnixSockets must be an array of nonempty strings")
        network["allowUnixSockets"] = [str(resolve_project_path(project, p, canonical=False)) for p in values]
    for name in ("allowUnixSockets", "allowMachLookup"):
        existing = network.get(name, [])
        if not isinstance(existing, list) or any(not isinstance(v, str) for v in existing):
            fail("Base network." + name + " must be an array of strings")
        network[name] = list(dict.fromkeys(existing + grants[name]))
    if messaging_paths:
        # SRT uses subpath filters for Unix bind/connect. Grant only the
        # project inbox directory, whose socket names vary per session.
        network["allowUnixSockets"] = list(dict.fromkeys(network["allowUnixSockets"] + messaging_paths))
    read_paths = [str(p) for p in agent_paths] + temp_paths + messaging_filesystem_paths
    read_paths += [executable, str(Path(executable).resolve())]
    read_paths += template_reads  # files the template links to, read-only
    tools = base_policy.get("tools")
    if venv is not None:
        read_paths += venv["allowRead"]
    if tools is not None:
        read_paths += tools["allowRead"]
    # Per-agent read grants (e.g. a Homebrew cask's helper binaries). Both
    # spellings, like global grants; never the home directory or an ancestor.
    for entry in profile["allowRead"]:
        for spelled in (resolve_project_path(project, entry, canonical=False), resolve_project_path(project, entry)):
            if spelled.is_relative_to(project) or account_home().is_relative_to(spelled):
                fail("agents." + agent + ".filesystem.allowRead cannot grant the project, your home or an ancestor: "
                     + str(spelled))
            read_paths.append(str(spelled))
    # Extra host tool directories (e.g. ~/.cargo/bin): readable, on PATH,
    # and write-denied below with every other PATH entry.
    extra_path = []
    project_launcher = grants.get("launcher", {})
    for entry in options.get("path", []) + profile["path"] + project_launcher.get("path", []):
        directory = resolve_project_path(project, entry, canonical=False)
        for spelled in (directory, directory.resolve()):
            if spelled.is_relative_to(project) or account_home().is_relative_to(spelled):
                fail("path (global or project) cannot add the project, your home or an ancestor: " + str(spelled))
            read_paths.append(str(spelled))
        if str(directory) not in extra_path:
            extra_path.append(str(directory))
    cache_paths = []
    cache = None
    merged_set_env = {**options.get("setEnv", {}), **project_launcher.get("setEnv", {}), **profile["setEnv"]}
    if any(uses_cache(value) for value in merged_set_env.values()):
        caches = account_home() / "Library/Caches"
        caches.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        # private_dir tightens every component it walks: start at Caches so
        # only srt-agent/<project> (ours) is created and chmod 0700.
        cache = private_dir(caches, Path("srt-agent") / project_cache_dir(project).name)
        cache_paths = list(dict.fromkeys([cache, cache.resolve()]))
        read_paths += [str(p) for p in cache_paths]
    for read_path in read_paths:
        reject_protected_grant(Path(read_path))
    launcher = Path(__file__).absolute()
    # Like bin/activate, the venv's bin wins every lookup. The shared tools
    # venv comes next, ahead of system Pythons, so python3 has its packages
    # in projects without a venv. path_protections write-denies them all.
    agent_path = list(dict.fromkeys(([venv["bin"]] if venv is not None else []) + [
        str(home / ".local/bin")] + ([tools["bin"]] if tools is not None else []) + extra_path + ["/opt/homebrew/bin", "/opt/homebrew/sbin",
        "/usr/local/bin", "/usr/local/sbin", "/usr/bin", "/bin", "/usr/sbin", "/sbin",
        str(Path(executable).parent),
    ]))
    path_dirs = path_protections(project, agent_path)
    # Protect source files as well as output: otherwise an agent could poison
    # the policy or launcher for the next invocation. Also protect anything
    # the user's own host tools will execute from the project (Git, direnv,
    # dotenv, VS Code) and every directory commands are looked up in.
    protected_paths = [
        policy_dir, settings_name, settings, override_path,
        # Launcher-owned: the identity record, and every other agent's tree
        # (writes are allow-listed anyway; this keeps them denied even if a
        # broader grant ever appears).
        storage / "project.json", *sibling_paths, storage / "srt-tmp",
        *group_protections(project, settings_name),
        template_directory(project, settings_name), template_directory(project, settings_name).resolve(),
        *template_protected, *[Path(t) for t in template_reads],
        *([Path(base_policy["base_settings"]["path"]), Path(base_policy["base_settings"]["resolved_path"])]
          if base_policy.get("base_settings") else []),
        *([storage / "shared"] if home_mode == "isolated" else []),
        launcher, launcher.resolve(), approval_directory().parent,
        *host_exec_protections(project),
        *path_dirs,
        *mandatory_denials(),
    ]
    if venv is not None:
        # Host-side python reads pyvenv.cfg on every start of this venv.
        protected_paths += [Path(venv["path"]) / "pyvenv.cfg", Path(venv["resolved"]) / "pyvenv.cfg"]
    if tools is not None:
        # Read-only for every agent, even if a later global grant would differ.
        protected_paths += [Path(tools["path"]), Path(tools["resolved"])]
    additions = {
        "denyRead": ["/", literal(account_home())] + [literal(p) for p in mandatory_denials()] + grants["denyRead"],
        "allowRead": [literal(p) for p in read_paths] + grants["allowRead"],
        "allowWrite": [literal(p) for p in agent_paths + temp_paths + messaging_filesystem_paths + cache_paths]
                      + grants["allowWrite"],
        "denyWrite": [literal(p) for p in protected_paths] + grants["denyWrite"],
    }
    # denyWrite beats allowWrite in srt: refuse to launch if a block covers
    # the agent's own home or temp, instead of failing later with EPERM.
    for needed in agent_paths + [Path(p) for p in temp_paths]:
        for blocked in additions["denyWrite"] + base_policy["filesystem"].get("denyWrite", []):
            text = blocked["path"] if isinstance(blocked, dict) else blocked
            if not (isinstance(blocked, str) and glob.has_magic(text)) and (
                    needed == Path(text) or needed.is_relative_to(text)):
                fail("denyWrite " + text + " covers the agent's own folder " + str(needed)
                     + "; in srt denyWrite wins, so the agent could not write its home or temp files")
    policy["filesystem"] = copy.deepcopy(base_policy["filesystem"])
    for name, entries in additions.items():
        policy["filesystem"][name] = unique_entries(policy["filesystem"].get(name, []) + entries)
    # Reads cannot be denied back once allowed (allowRead beats denyRead), so
    # sibling agents and other projects stay unreadable only if no grant
    # covers the storage roots. Refuse any grant that overlaps them, other
    # than the launcher's own per-agent and per-project entries.
    own = {str(p) for p in agent_paths + cache_paths} | set(temp_paths) | set(messaging_filesystem_paths)
    roots = list(dict.fromkeys(p for base_dir in (storage_base(), cache_base()) for p in (base_dir, base_dir.resolve())))
    for name in ("allowRead", "allowWrite"):
        for entry in policy["filesystem"][name]:
            text = entry["path"] if isinstance(entry, dict) else entry
            if text in own:
                continue
            if isinstance(entry, str) and glob.has_magic(text):
                # Every match lies under the last complete folder before the
                # first wildcard (*, ?, [), even for a partial name like
                # ~/.local/sha*: check that folder.
                magic = min(i for i in (text.find(c) for c in "*?[") if i >= 0)
                candidate = Path(text[:magic].rsplit("/", 1)[0] or "/")
            else:
                candidate = Path(text)
            # Lexical '..' must not hide an overlap.
            candidate = Path(os.path.normpath(candidate))
            if allow_home and candidate == account_home():
                continue  # --allow-home: documented to expose all agent storage
            for root in roots:
                if candidate == root or candidate.is_relative_to(root) or root.is_relative_to(candidate):
                    fail(name + " grant overlaps agent storage (other agents or projects would become reachable): "
                         + text)
    refuse_ineffective_read_blocks(policy["filesystem"]["allowRead"],
                                   list(base_policy["filesystem"].get("denyRead", [])) + list(grants["denyRead"]))
    policy_path = write_policy(policy_dir, agent, policy)
    child_env = {variable: str(home / relative) for variable, relative in homes.items()}
    child_env.update({
        "HOME": str(home),
        "XDG_CONFIG_HOME": str(home / ".config"),
        "XDG_CACHE_HOME": str(home / ".cache"),
        "XDG_DATA_HOME": str(home / ".local/share"),
        "XDG_STATE_HOME": str(home / ".local/state"),
        "XDG_RUNTIME_DIR": str(temp_link / "run"),
        "PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX": str(home / ".cache/python"),
        "PYTHONUSERBASE": str(home / ".local"),
        "NPM_CONFIG_CACHE": str(home / ".npm"),
        "NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG": str(home / ".npmrc"),
        "PIP_CACHE_DIR": str(home / ".cache/pip"),
        "CARGO_HOME": str(home / ".cargo"),
        "RUSTUP_HOME": str(home / ".rustup"),
        "TMPDIR": str(temp), "TMP": str(temp), "TEMP": str(temp),
        "CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR": str(temp),
        "ZDOTDIR": str(home),
        "PATH": ":".join(agent_path),
    })
    if venv is not None:
        child_env["VIRTUAL_ENV"] = venv["path"]
        prompt = os.environ.get("VIRTUAL_ENV_PROMPT", "") if os.environ.get("VIRTUAL_ENV") else ""
        child_env["VIRTUAL_ENV_PROMPT"] = prompt.replace("\0", "") or Path(venv["path"]).name
    # Global setEnv, then the project's, then the agent's own; a leading ~/
    # means your account home (e.g. RUSTUP_HOME).
    for name, value in {**options.get("setEnv", {}), **project_launcher.get("setEnv", {}),
                        **profile["setEnv"]}.items():
        if name in child_env and name not in OVERRIDABLE_ENV:
            fail("setEnv cannot override launcher-managed " + name)
        if name in CACHE_ONLY_ENV:
            if not uses_cache(value):
                fail(name + " may only be set to a {cache} folder, e.g. \"{cache}/tmp\"")
            rest = value[len(CACHE_PLACEHOLDER):].lstrip("/")
            expand_env_value(value, project)  # rejects ".." before any mkdir
            # Must exist before tools use it; O_NOFOLLOW walk, so a symlink
            # planted in the agent-writable cache cannot redirect the mkdir.
            if rest:
                private_dir(cache, rest)
        child_env[name] = expand_env_value(value, project)
        if name == "TMPDIR":
            # Keep the aliases consistent for tools that read TMP/TEMP.
            child_env["TMP"] = child_env["TEMP"] = child_env[name]
    patterns = BASE_PASS_ENV + profile["passEnv"] + options["passEnv"]
    passed = passthrough_env(patterns, child_env)
    # srt runs on the host. Give it the real HOME and a PATH without any
    # agent-writable directory: srt is a node script started via env, and a
    # planted <agent home>/.local/bin/node would otherwise run unsandboxed.
    # The private HOME/PATH are applied inside the sandbox by EXEC_CODE.
    env = dict(passed)
    env.update({
        "HOME": str(account_home()),
        "PATH": host_path(project),
        # Only srt itself needs the short path for its pre-sandbox Unix
        # sockets; it is launcher-owned, never the agent-writable tmp.
        "TMPDIR": str(host_temp_link),
        "SRT_AGENT_CHILD_ENV": json.dumps(child_env, ensure_ascii=True),
    })
    # The in-sandbox wrapper is /usr/bin/python3, which on macOS is an
    # xcode-select stub: without DEVELOPER_DIR it reads the
    # /var/select/developer_dir link before the agent environment exists.
    # Hand it the same DEVELOPER_DIR the agent gets, so /var need not be
    # readable.
    if "DEVELOPER_DIR" in child_env:
        env["DEVELOPER_DIR"] = child_env["DEVELOPER_DIR"]
    return (srt, executable, policy_path, child_env, env, temp, messaging, profile, sorted(passed), path_dirs, venv,
            base_policy.get("tools"), agent_root, home_mode)


def sandbox_python(child_env):
    # /usr/bin/python3 is an xcode-select stub: it reads /var/select (unless
    # DEVELOPER_DIR is set) and writes an xcrun cache to the per-user temp
    # folder, both rightly outside the sandbox. With DEVELOPER_DIR, run the
    # real interpreter inside it instead, but only a root-owned file that
    # neither group nor others can write, reached through root-owned folders
    # (the same Apple Python the stub would start).
    developer = child_env.get("DEVELOPER_DIR")
    if not developer:
        return "/usr/bin/python3"
    candidate = Path(developer) / "usr/bin/python3"
    try:
        real = candidate.resolve(strict=True)
        for item in [real, *real.parents]:
            info = item.stat()
            if info.st_uid != 0 or info.st_mode & 0o022:
                raise PermissionError(str(item) + " is not root-owned and write-protected")
        if not stat.S_ISREG(real.stat().st_mode) or not os.access(real, os.X_OK):
            raise PermissionError(str(real) + " is not an executable file")
    except OSError as error:
        print("srt-agent: warning: not using " + str(candidate) + " (" + str(error) + "); falling back to "
              "/usr/bin/python3, which may print xcrun cache errors", file=sys.stderr)
        return "/usr/bin/python3"
    return str(real)


def parse_cli(argv):
    # Establish the boundary before argparse can consume or discard it.
    # The right-hand side is opaque, even when it names launcher options.
    argv = list(argv)
    if "--" in argv:
        separator = argv.index("--")
        launcher_argv, forwarded = argv[:separator], argv[separator + 1:]
    else:
        launcher_argv, forwarded = argv, []
    # Suppress inherited defaults so common options work before a subcommand
    # or after its leaf without a later parser resetting an earlier value.
    common = argparse.ArgumentParser(add_help=False, allow_abbrev=False)
    common.add_argument("--allow-home", action="store_true", default=argparse.SUPPRESS,
                        help="Permit home launches and approved home-wide reads for this invocation")
    common.add_argument("--project", default=argparse.SUPPRESS,
                        help="Use this project root instead of Git root/current directory")
    common.add_argument("--settings", default=argparse.SUPPRESS,
                        help="Global srt-agent config (default: SRT_AGENT_SETTINGS or ~/.config/srt-agent/config.jsonc)")
    venv = common.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    venv.add_argument("--auto-venv", dest="venv_mode", action="store_const", const="auto", default=argparse.SUPPRESS,
                      help="Without VIRTUAL_ENV, use the project's .venv if present")
    venv.add_argument("--no-auto-venv", dest="venv_mode", action="store_const", const="env", default=argparse.SUPPRESS,
                      help="Use only an activated VIRTUAL_ENV, overriding global autoVenv")
    venv.add_argument("--no-venv", dest="venv_mode", action="store_const", const="off", default=argparse.SUPPRESS,
                      help="Ignore VIRTUAL_ENV and any .venv for this invocation")
    parser =argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, parents=[common], allow_abbrev=False,
                                     formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    commands = parser.add_subparsers(dest="command", required=True)
    project_parser = commands.add_parser("project", parents=[common], allow_abbrev=False, help="Manage project configuration and approval")
    actions = project_parser.add_subparsers(dest="project_action", required=True)
    for action, description in (
        ("init", "Create the project override without replacing an existing file"),
        ("approve", "Review and approve this project's current configuration"),
        ("revoke", "Revoke this project's saved approval"),
    ):
        action_parser = actions.add_parser(action, parents=[common], allow_abbrev=False, help=description, description=description)
        if action == "init":
            action_parser.add_argument("-e", "--extends", metavar="GROUP", action="append", default=[],
                                       help="Group from the global groups to extend (repeatable or "
                                            "comma-separated), e.g. --extends rust,python")
    group_parser = commands.add_parser("group", parents=[common], allow_abbrev=False,
                                       help="Generate group files for tools")
    group_actions = group_parser.add_subparsers(dest="group_action", required=True)
    create = group_actions.add_parser("create", parents=[common], allow_abbrev=False,
                                      help="Write groups/<name>.jsonc granting what the tools need to read")
    create.add_argument("name", nargs="?", metavar="NAME", help="Group name (default for one tool: tool/<tool>)")
    create.add_argument("--tool", action="append", required=True, metavar="PROGRAM",
                        help="Program name on PATH or a path (repeatable)")
    create.add_argument("--force", action="store_true", help="Replace an existing group file")
    update = group_actions.add_parser("update", parents=[common], allow_abbrev=False,
                                      help="Regenerate a group made by group create")
    update.add_argument("name", metavar="NAME")
    run = commands.add_parser("run", parents=[common], allow_abbrev=False, help="Run a coding agent inside srt")
    mode = run.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    mode.add_argument("--show", action="store_true", help="Preview effective paths/policy without launching or approving")
    mode.add_argument("--check", action="store_true", help="Test filesystem protections inside srt without starting an agent")
    run.add_argument("-l", "--allow-local-binding", action="store_true", help="Allow local listeners/loopback for this launch (e.g. login, dsh web)")
    run.add_argument("--no-pty-isolation", action="store_true",
                     help="Attach the agent directly to this terminal instead of a fresh pseudo-terminal")
    messaging = run.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    messaging.add_argument("--cross-session-messaging", dest="allow_cross_session_messaging", choices=("off", "project", "global"), default=None,
                           help="Claude only: select communication scope for this run (overrides the global default)")
    messaging.add_argument("--allow-cross-session-messaging", dest="allow_cross_session_messaging", action="store_const", const="project", default=None,
                           help="Alias for --cross-session-messaging project")
    messaging.add_argument("--no-cross-session-messaging", dest="allow_cross_session_messaging", action="store_const", const="off", default=None,
                           help="Disable launcher messaging support for this run, overriding the global default")
    run.add_argument("agent", metavar="AGENT",
                     help="Agent to run: " + ", ".join(sorted(AGENTS)) + ", deepseek (alias of dsh), or one from agents")
    run.add_argument("--resume", nargs="?", const="", default=None, metavar="SESSION_ID",
                     help="Claude only: forward --resume and optional session ID without requiring --")
    run.epilog = "Agent arguments must follow --. Example: srt-agent run claude -- --model sonnet"
    execute = commands.add_parser("exec", parents=[common], allow_abbrev=False,
                                  help="Run a command, or your shell, with an agent's sandbox and environment")
    execute.add_argument("--show", action="store_true", help="Preview effective paths/policy without launching or approving")
    execute.add_argument("-l", "--allow-local-binding", action="store_true", help="Allow local listeners/loopback for this launch")
    execute.add_argument("--no-pty-isolation", action="store_true",
                         help="Attach the command directly to this terminal instead of a fresh pseudo-terminal")
    execute.add_argument("agent", metavar="AGENT", help="Agent whose sandbox, HOME and environment to use")
    execute.epilog = "The command must follow --; without one, $SHELL starts. Example: srt-agent exec claude -- pytest -q"
    args = parser.parse_args(launcher_argv)
    for name, default in (("allow_home", False), ("project", None), ("settings", None), ("venv_mode", None)):
        if not hasattr(args, name):
            setattr(args, name, default)
    if args.command == "exec":
        args.agent = AGENT_ALIASES.get(args.agent, args.agent)
        if not AGENT_NAME.match(args.agent) or args.agent in RESERVED_AGENT_NAMES:
            parser.error("invalid agent name: " + args.agent)
        args.check = False
        args.allow_cross_session_messaging = "off"
        args.custom_messaging_socket = False
        args.agent_args = forwarded
    elif args.command == "run":
        args.agent = AGENT_ALIASES.get(args.agent, args.agent)
        if not AGENT_NAME.match(args.agent) or args.agent in RESERVED_AGENT_NAMES:
            parser.error("invalid agent name: " + args.agent)
        args.custom_messaging_socket = any(
            value == "--messaging-socket-path" or value.startswith("--messaging-socket-path=")
            for value in forwarded
        )
        if args.allow_cross_session_messaging not in (None, "off"):
            if args.agent != "claude":
                parser.error("--allow-cross-session-messaging is supported for Claude only")
            if args.custom_messaging_socket:
                parser.error("--allow-cross-session-messaging cannot be combined with an agent --messaging-socket-path override")
        if args.resume is not None and not AGENTS.get(args.agent, {}).get("resumeShorthand"):
            parser.error("--resume shorthand is for Claude; pass agent flags after --, e.g. run codex -- resume --last")
        shorthand = [] if args.resume is None else ["--resume"] + ([args.resume] if args.resume else [])
        args.agent_args = shorthand + forwarded
    elif forwarded:
        parser.error("Only run and exec accept arguments after --")
    return args


def srt_independence_probe(policy):
    # --check only: find a domain that srt's own ~/.srt-settings.json allows
    # but this launch's generated policy does not. That file is read solely
    # for this comparison, never as policy input.
    try:
        data = parse_jsonc(read_regular(account_home() / ".srt-settings.json"), "~/.srt-settings.json")
        network = data.get("network", {}) if isinstance(data, dict) else {}
        theirs, their_denied = network.get("allowedDomains", []), network.get("deniedDomains", [])
        generated = json.loads(Path(policy).read_text()).get("network", {})
        ours = list(generated.get("allowedDomains", [])) + list(generated.get("deniedDomains", []))
    except (OSError, RuntimeError, ValueError, AttributeError, TypeError):
        return ""

    def covers(pattern, domain):
        # Conservative: *.x is treated as covering x too, so a domain the
        # generated policy might allow or deny is never used as the probe.
        if not isinstance(pattern, str):
            return False
        pattern, domain = pattern.lower().rstrip("."), domain.lower().rstrip(".")
        if pattern.startswith("*."):
            pattern = pattern[2:]
        return domain == pattern or domain.endswith("." + pattern)

    excluded = ours + (their_denied if isinstance(their_denied, list) else [])
    for domain in theirs if isinstance(theirs, list) else []:
        if (isinstance(domain, str) and "*" not in domain and re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9.-]+", domain)
                and not any(covers(pattern, domain) for pattern in excluded)):
            return domain
    return ""


def default_shell(project):
    # The host's login shell, unless it is missing or lives in the project.
    shell = os.environ.get("SHELL", "")
    if os.path.isabs(shell) and os.access(shell, os.X_OK) and not Path(shell).resolve().is_relative_to(project):
        return shell
    return "/bin/zsh"


def main(argv=None):
    os.umask(0o077)
    args = parse_cli(sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv)
    settings = args.settings or os.environ.get("SRT_AGENT_SETTINGS") or str(account_home() / GLOBAL_SETTINGS)
    if not args.settings and not os.environ.get("SRT_AGENT_SETTINGS") and not os.path.lexists(settings):
        fail("No global srt-agent config at " + settings)
    if args.command == "group":
        if os.environ.get("SANDBOX_RUNTIME") == "1":
            fail("Groups must be managed outside a running sandbox")
        if args.group_action == "create":
            create_tool_group(settings, args.name, args.tool, force=args.force)
        else:
            update_tool_group(settings, args.name)
        return
    if args.command == "project":
        project = project_root(args.project, allow_home=args.allow_home)
        if args.project_action == "init":
            init_project(project, settings, args.extends)
        elif args.project_action == "revoke":
            revoke_approval(project)
        else:
            path, grants, data, raw = project_permissions(project, settings, allow_home=args.allow_home)
            base_policy = load_base_policy(project, settings, allow_home=args.allow_home, removals=grants["remove"])
            mode = venv_mode(args.venv_mode, base_policy["launcher_options"])
            venv = detect_virtualenv(project, mode)
            require_approval(project, path, raw, data, grants, base_policy, allow_home=args.allow_home,
                             venv=venv, mode=mode)
            print("Project settings are approved:", project)
            if venv is not None:
                print("Virtualenv is approved:", venv["path"])
        return
    if sys.platform != "darwin":
        fail("This policy is for macOS; adapt system read paths before using it elsewhere")
    agent_args = args.agent_args
    allow_home = args.allow_home
    project = project_root(args.project, allow_home=allow_home)
    srt, executable, policy, child_env, env, temp, messaging, profile, passed, path_dirs, venv, tools, agent_root, home_mode = prepare(
        args.agent, project, settings, allow_local_binding=args.allow_local_binding,
        require_project_approval=not args.show,
        allow_home=allow_home,
        allow_cross_session_messaging=args.allow_cross_session_messaging,
        custom_messaging_socket=args.custom_messaging_socket,
        # exec runs no agent session, so leave Claude's registry untouched.
        activate_messaging=not args.show and args.command == "run",
        requested_venv_mode=args.venv_mode,
    )
    messaging_directory = messaging["directory"]
    if args.command == "exec":
        # Resolved by execvpe inside the sandbox against the agent PATH, so
        # venv commands such as pytest are found without a full path.
        agent_args = agent_args or [default_shell(project)]
    elif messaging_directory:
        # An explicit existing private leaf avoids Claude's automatic
        # directory vet, which needs to read symlink ancestors outside the
        # granted temp subtree. Never substitute a long realpath: macOS
        # Unix socket names are limited to roughly 104 bytes.
        socket_path = Path(messaging_directory) / (os.urandom(8).hex() + ".sock")
        if len(os.fsencode(socket_path)) > 103:
            fail("Messaging socket path exceeds the macOS Unix socket limit: " + str(socket_path))
        agent_args = ["--messaging-socket-path", str(socket_path)] + agent_args
    if args.command == "run":
        for flag in reversed(profile.get("prependArgs", [])):
            if flag not in agent_args:
                agent_args = [flag] + agent_args
    python = sandbox_python(child_env)
    prefix = [srt, "--settings", str(policy), "--", python, "-I", "-c"]
    if args.command == "exec":
        command = prefix + [EXEC_CODE] + agent_args
    else:
        command = prefix + [EXEC_CODE, executable] + agent_args
    if args.check:
        # Run the probes through the same entrypoint as the agent.
        command = prefix + [EXEC_CODE, python, "-I", "-c", CHECK_CODE,
                   str(policy), str(Path(__file__).absolute()),
                   str(project_settings_path(project)), str(Path(settings).expanduser().absolute()),
                   str(approval_directory().parent),
                   messaging_directory or "", messaging["registry"] or "", str(project),
                   json.dumps([str(p) for p in path_dirs]),
                   json.dumps({
                       "identity": str(agent_root.parent.parent / "project.json"),
                       "host_temp": str(agent_root.parent.parent / "srt-tmp" / agent_root.name),
                       "shared_home": str(agent_root.parent.parent / "shared")
                                      if not Path(child_env["HOME"]).is_relative_to(agent_root.parent.parent / "shared") else "",
                       "storage_base": str(storage_base()),
                       "cache_base": str(cache_base()) if cache_base().is_dir() else "",
                       "siblings": [{"path": str(agent_root.parent / name), "exists": (agent_root.parent / name).is_dir()}
                                    for name in sorted(set(AGENTS) | {e.name for e in agent_root.parent.iterdir()})
                                    if name != agent_root.name],
                   }),
                   srt_independence_probe(policy)]
    elif not args.no_pty_isolation and not args.show:
        env["SRT_AGENT_PTY"] = "1"
    if args.show:
        with policy.open() as handle:
            effective = json.load(handle)
        print(json.dumps({"project": str(project), "agent": args.agent, "temporary_files": str(temp),
                          "cross_session_messaging": messaging, "virtual_env": venv, "tools_venv": tools,
                          "agent_storage": str(agent_root), "agent_groups": profile.get("groups", []),
                          "template_files": profile.get("template", []),
                          "agent_home": {"mode": home_mode, "path": child_env["HOME"]},
                          "environment": child_env, "passed_host_variables": passed,
                          "command": [part if part not in (EXEC_CODE, CHECK_CODE) else "<inline python>" for part in command],
                          "policy": effective}, indent=2))
        return
    if args.allow_local_binding:
        print("srt-agent: --allow-local-binding also lets the agent reach every service listening on localhost.",
              file=sys.stderr)
    if args.project:
        os.chdir(project)
    # exec keeps the real TTY and signals; do not pipe interactive agent I/O.
    os.execve(srt, command, env)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        main()
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        print("\nsrt-agent: cancelled.", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(130)
    except (RuntimeError, OSError, ValueError) as error:
        print("srt-agent: " + str(error), file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(1)

